PVD("kiribati_ndp_2024-2027",{"docs":["","KIR NDP 2024 2027"],"s":{"1":[[1,"6","10","Sustainable Tourism and Cultural Industry Development","Foster and strengthen sustainable tourism and cultural industry development.",""],[1,"6","11","Value-Added Processing for Product Development and Diversification","3. Promote product development and diversification through Value-Added Processing.",""],[1,"6","12","Business Environment Improvement for Private and Foreign Investment","Create a favorable and sustainable business environment for both private and foreign investment.",""],[1,"61","1","Product Diversification for Export Promotion","Through product diversification strategies, the Government is firmly committed to increasing the export of locally made products including value-added products mainly from fish, copra and coconut.",""],[1,"62","2","Value-Added Fisheries and Agriculture Production Promotion","Promoting value-added production, particularly in fisheries and agriculture, to diversify exports beyond raw commodities",""],[1,"62","4","SME and Entrepreneur Credit Access Enhancement","Enhancing credit access to Small and Medium-sized enterprises and entrepreneurs to overcome financing barriers",""],[1,"62","5","Business Law and Approval Process Streamlining","Streamlining business laws and approval processes to improve the investment (currently ranked 164/190 in Ease of Doing Business)",""],[1,"63","12","Business Registration Simplification and Investment Incentive Package","Simplifying business registration, enhancing legal frameworks and offering clear investment incentives, tax breaks and public private partnership opportunities to encourage foreign investors.",""],[1,"64","1","Joint Venture Promotion in Key Sectors","Encouraging joint ventures in key sectors like fisheries, tourism, agriculture and renewable energy.",""],[1,"64","3","Land Access and Leasing Reform for Foreign Investment","To enhance foreign direct investment, the government must implement policies that simplify land access, ensure transparency, strengthen land-use planning and create friendly leasing mechanisms.",""],[1,"64","4","Strengthening Inter-Ministerial Investment Coordination","In Kiribati, strengthening inter-ministerial coordination ensures that investment policies are aligned, approvals are streamlined, and investors receive clear and consistent guidance.",""],[1,"64","11","Blue Economy Sector Expansion","Diversify its economy by expanding blue economy sectors (i.e., marine research and eco-tourism)",""],[1,"147","36","Expansion of Financing Support for Business Start-Ups and Business Expansion","Increase the number of financial institutions provides support financing for business start-ups & business expansion",""]],"2":[[1,"5","10","Civil Servant Capacity Building Programme","Capacity building for civil servants - Strengthening the skills and competencies through education and training in Kiribati as well as overseas.",""],[1,"6","2","Human Resource Development Systems and Strategies Strengthening","Strengthen and enhance HRD systems/strategies that promote continuous learning and address current and future skill gaps.",""],[1,"6","3","Public Sector Performance Management Strengthening","Improve and strengthen public sector performance management.",""],[1,"6","4","Strategic Public Service Workforce Planning","Develop a strategic workforce plan for the public service.",""],[1,"49","2","Public Service Transformation Reform","The Government, through the PSO, is committed to transforming the public service by strengthening human capital, improving performance management, and adopting innovative approaches.","PSO"],[1,"49","2","Public Service Capacity and Performance Systems Reform","Reforms will target policy development, training, workforce planning, and performance systems to enhance efficiency, accountability, and responsiveness.",""],[1,"49","3","Flexible Public Sector Workforce Training Programs","The Kiribati Institute of Technology (KIT) also plays a key role in delivering flexible training programs that accommodate the diverse needs of the public sector workforce.",""],[1,"49","4","Public Service Capacity Development and Training Programme","the PSO will continue to implement long-term (academic) and short-term training to bridge the current skill gap and prepare the workforce with future needs",""],[1,"49","4","Training Partner and Donor Mobilization for Capacity Development","it will also explore training partners/donors to support capacity development",""],[1,"49","5","Customized Training for Public and Private Sector Workers and the Public","KIT provides customized training for public and private sector workers and the public.",""],[1,"49","6","Skills Training Strategy for Service Delivery Needs","Training strategies will focus on enhancing both foundational and specialized skills aligned with evolving service delivery needs.",""],[1,"49","7","Human Resource Development Strategy Strengthening","To enhance capacity development, the Human Resource Development strategy needs to be strengthened to provide the best HR interventions to ensure there's availability of skills required from time to time.",""],[1,"49","7","Human Resource Development Data Input and Analysis System","HRD data input is critical for analysis to ensure that the critical skill gaps identified are realistic and the HRD strategy developed is effective.",""],[1,"49","8","Public Service Skills Gap Survey","Conducting a skill gap survey to employees is a means to ensure that relevant and realistic data is collected.",""],[1,"49","9","Staff Performance Appraisal System Review and Improvement","A comprehensive review, now 90% complete, is underway to improve the system's usability, relevance, and effectiveness by adapting globally recognized best practices.",""],[1,"50","8","Public Service Workforce Strategy Development","The strategies in addressing the public service workforce challenges/issues will be developed and become the Public Service Workforce Strategy which its sole purpose is to outline how the current/future challenges will be addressed over the course of 4 years.",""],[1,"50","10","Workforce Data Collection and Analysis","Collect and analyze workforce data to draw key insights and identify critical areas to be addressed",""],[1,"50","11","Workforce Strategy Development and Implementation","Develop and implement workforce strategy to address succession risks, skill gaps and workforce challenges",""],[1,"50","12","Workforce Planning Integration into Capacity Development Initiatives","Integrate workforce planning into capacity development initiatives",""],[1,"50","13","Human Resource Development Strategy Strengthening","Strengthen the HRD strategy to improve capacity development and to bridge skill gap challenges through short, medium, and long-term training",""],[1,"50","14","Public Service Employee Engagement Programmes","Develop and implement employee engagement programs to boost motivation and morale of the public service",""],[1,"50","15","Performance Monitoring and Evaluation Strengthening","Strengthen performance monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"111","2","Governance Strengthening Initiative","This Kiribati Development Plan (KDP) aims to strengthen governance at all levels, from local communities to the broader public sector.",""],[1,"112","19","Technical and Financial Support for Good Governance Capacity","Technical and Financial Support; to enhance the government's capacity in advancing good governance in Kiribati.",""],[1,"119","4","Public Sector Human Resource Policy Enforcement","Additionally, it is responsible for enforcing and implementing human resource policies and regulations.",""],[1,"120","17","Customer Service and Institutional Orientation Training","Induction and refresher training on Customer Service, National Conditions of Service (NCS), organizational structure, and ministerial roles.",""],[1,"123","7","Government Support and Funding for Workforce Policy and Capacity Building","better government support and funding in developing policies and capacity building will ensure that a decent, equitable and inclusive workforce is realized throughout Kiribati.",""],[1,"147","13","Strategic Workforce Plan for the Public Service","Develop a Strategic workforce plan for the public service",""]],"3":[[1,"8","3","Land Administration and Planning Policy Strengthening","Strengthen land administration and planning policies and practices, including efficient land allocation for diverse purposes, to build a dynamic, environmentally sustainable urban economy while supporting rural development and environmental.",""],[1,"98","6","Land Management Services Delivery","The Land Management Division continues to deliver land management services to serve the development demands of the government as well as the private sector through conduction of land surveys, the provision of accurate land ownership information including updating of land information and attending court proceedings related to land issues.",""],[1,"98","6","Survey Department Capacity Strengthening","Some of the key achievements being achieved for land management and administration include strengthened capacity of the Survey department to undertake land survey through procurement of specialized survey equipment, increased monitoring to enhance compliance of development to approved national general land use",""],[1,"99","1","Kiribati Lands Information System Upgrade","The initiative to improve land information storage system through the upgrading of the Kiribati Lands Information system (KLIS) was also progressed",""],[1,"99","1","Land Survey Services Expansion","Gradual progress continues to be delivered for land surveys conducted to serve the increased demand from the government as well as the private sector.",""],[1,"104","7","Strengthening Land Administration and Planning","Improving land administration requires the ongoing strengthening of land administration and planning, including efficiency in land allocation to accommodate diverse development purposes.",""],[1,"104","7","Land Administration Staff Capacity Building and Professional Training","Capacity building and professional training of staff are a high priority need to ensure that staff are equipped with skills on how to perform effective land administration services to enhance sustainable development.",""],[1,"104","7","Technical Capacity and Land Management Coordination Investment","Ongoing investment is required in technical capacity, the provision of specialized equipment, improving coordination of land management activities across different authorities and ensuring compliance with proper land use development and regulations.",""],[1,"105","1","Land Survey Equipment Provision","The provision of land survey equipment is also required to ensure the accuracy of the land survey and the provision of accurate land information.",""],[1,"105","1","Land Survey Skills Development and Training","To achieve this, staff need to possess advanced skills on how to conduct land surveys effectively with industry standards and technological innovations while enhancing productivity and service delivery and to improve capacity in conducting surveys to address the demand of government and the private sector development needs.",""],[1,"105","1","Continuous Professional Development for Land Administration Staff","Professional capacity building and training is also a priority need that needs to be addressed.",""],[1,"105","2","Land Management Capacity Building and Systems Upgrade","Capacity building is required to ensure that staff are equipped with skills on how to perform and deliver quality land administration services, including the provision of specialized equipment, the development of land information systems and databases, improving coordination of land management activities across different authorities and ensuring compliance with proper land use development and regulations.",""],[1,"105","2","Comprehensive Land Management Planning for Squatter Settlement Response","Capacity building and the development of comprehensive land management plans are needed to address the growing issue of squatter settlements and improve land governance.",""],[1,"105","2","Land Use Planning Update and Procedure Streamlining","Other activities in line with the enhancement of services from the Land Management Division include the update to the GLUP and streamlining all procedures in line with existing laws/legislations - this task will require the assistance of mentors or technical assistance.",""],[1,"105","2","Standard Operating Procedures for Land Management Services","This Standard Operational Procedures or SOPs aims to develop set criteria which will draw clear cut instructions aimed at better service delivery for the public.",""],[1,"105","2","Land Law Review and Harmonization Initiative","The Land Management Division also needs to review and upgrade existing land laws and legislations to fit the context present today and in order to synchronize land laws/legislations with other relevant laws/legislations such as the Environment Act, Building Act and so forth.",""],[1,"105","2","GIS and Surveyor Training Programme","Trainings to GIS & Surveyors is also crucial to the Land Management Division as technology is evolving every day and the GIS and Surveyors team needs to undertake regular training for land management divisions to remain effective in today's rapidly evolving technological landscape.",""],[1,"151","29","Land Administration and Planning Strengthening","Stregthen land administration and planning, including efficient land allocation for diverse purposes, to build a dynamic, environmentally sustainable urban economy while supporting rural development",""]],"4":[[1,"21","4","Enhanced Metadata Tool for Monitoring and Reporting","For KDP (2024-2027), the tool has been further enhanced into an intuitive and user- friendly system designed to supports informed policy decisions, strengthen accountability, and promotes the effective execution of the KDP.",""],[1,"22","3","Cross-Sector Monitoring and Evaluation Strengthening","This initiative reflects the Government's broader strategy to embed robust monitoring and evaluation practices across all sectors, thereby ensuring that the implementation of the KDP remains focused, measurable, and aligned with national development priorities.",""],[1,"22","6","Stakeholder Consultation for Framework Development","The Government proactively sought input from State-Owned Enterprises (SOEs), private businesses through the Kiribati Chamber of Commerce and Industry (KCCI), churches, and Non-Governmental Organizations (NGOs).",""],[1,"22","6","Zero Draft Public Feedback Process","Participants were also informed that the Zero Draft of the KDP would be shared with them for feedback following Cabinet endorsement - a measure designed to reinforce transparency, accountability, and public ownership of the plan.",""],[1,"24","7","Metadata Tool Training and Capacity-Building","As such, more comprehensive and ongoing training is needed to ensure that all stakeholders, particularly those in key ministries, are fully equipped to utilize the tool effectively.",""],[1,"24","7","Metadata Tool for Progress Tracking","One of the key tools introduced to address this challenge was the Metadata tool, designed to streamline the tracking of progress and improve data consistency.",""],[1,"25","4","KDP Framework Outcome Tracking Enhancement","As part of the ongoing effort to improve the KDP framework, a critical enhancement was made with the addition of an \"Outcome\" column.",""],[1,"26","5","DIME Taskforce Implementation Coordination Mechanism","At the heart of this implementation strategy is the DIME Taskforce, whose members will serve as key facilitators in bridging Ministries, Departments, and a broad range of stakeholders throughout the four-year implementation period.",""],[1,"26","6","DIME Taskforce Coordination and Monitoring Mechanism","DIME Taskforce members will play a proactive role in fostering continuous dialogue between government entities and external partners.",""],[1,"26","7","Plan Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","A robust Monitoring and Evaluation (M&E) framework, detailed in Annex 5, underpins the implementation of the Plan.",""],[1,"26","8","Regular Performance Review and Public Reporting System","This system of regular tracking and performance assessment will not only support internal learning and adaptive management but will also inform public reporting and policy review processes.",""],[1,"27","1","Multi-stakeholder Development Implementation and Localization","Achieving the ambitious targets set forth in the Plan will require the active engagement and cooperation of all sectors of society - including political and traditional leaders, public servants, community-based organizations, faith-based institutions, businesses, and individual citizens.",""],[1,"28","5","Donor Project Alignment and Analysis at NEPO","The Government will work to ensure that development partners' activities and projects are better aligned with the priorities set out in the new KDP.",""],[1,"28","7","NEPO Central Coordination Point for Development Partners","The KDP seeks to improve the relationship between development partners and the Government by clearly defining NEPO as the central point of contact for all development-related matters.",""],[1,"28","7","Early NEPO Involvement in Project Planning","NEPO will be involved early in the planning and discussion of new projects with line Ministries.","line Ministries"],[1,"28","8","High-Level Oversight of Development Partners' Projects","3. Strengthen High-Level Oversight of Development Partners' Projects",""],[1,"28","9","Project Review and Cabinet Submission Oversight Mechanism","the KDP establishes the requirement that all projects, whether fully or partly funded by development partners, be presented to NEPO for assessment.",""],[1,"28","10","Government of Kiribati Donor Committee","4. Establish the Government of Kiribati Donor Committee",""],[1,"28","11","Government of Kiribati Donor Committee","the KDP proposes the establishment of a Government of Kiribati Donor Committee.",""],[1,"28","12","Development Partner Coordination and Alignment Mechanism","Through improved coordination, oversight, and alignment with national priorities, the Government of Kiribati (GoK) aims to build a more sustainable and resilient future with the support of its development partners.","Government of Kiribati (GoK)"],[1,"29","8","Annual KDP Performance Reporting","NEPO will prepare a report on the KDP, and its performance, as part of annual budgeting processes.",""],[1,"29","9","Integrated Budgeting and Planning Mainstreaming of KDP","Integrating budgeting and planning will mainstream the new KDP across the whole of Government which will facilitate its implementation and monitoring.",""],[1,"71","2","International Support Mobilization for National Priorities","The government strategically mobilizes international support through soft loans, bilateral grants, and regional programs to fund national priorities while maintaining debt sustainability.",""],[1,"71","4","Domestic Fiscal Capacity Strengthening and Financial Management Reform","By aligning external funding with national priorities and strengthening financial management institutions and systems, Kiribati aims to gradually reduce its reliance on development assistance while continuing to deliver essential services and hardship alleviation programs.",""],[1,"148","23","Financial Instruments Access and Aid Coordination Strengthening","Strengthen access to financial instruments and improve aid coordination",""]],"5":[[1,"8","8","Anti-Corruption Legal and Regulatory Strengthening","The Government of Kiribati aims for a corrupt-free society through the strengthening of its legislative and regulatory frameworks, as well as ensuring effective enforcement and compliance with these frameworks.",""],[1,"8","8","Institutional Independence for Good Governance","This includes enhancing the independence of institutions to promote good governance and eliminate corruption.",""],[1,"8","10","Legal Sector and Institutional Strengthening","Strengthen and enhance legal sectors and institutions.",""],[1,"110","2","Institutional Strengthening for Anti-Corruption Compliance","The Government of Kiribati is committed to fostering a corruption-free society by strengthening institutions that enforce and uphold compliance with governance frameworks.",""],[1,"110","11","Access to Justice and Good Governance Advocacy","This commitment is reflected in Kiribati's ongoing advocacy for improved access to justice, law, and order, as well as its leadership in promoting good governance and anti-corruption initiatives, both regionally and internationally through the Te Ieniwa Vision.",""],[1,"110","13","Anti-Corruption Preparedness and Institutional Strengthening Measures","The government must take proactive measures to strengthen preparedness programs, legal frameworks, institutions, and access to justice to mitigate the risks of corrupt practices.",""],[1,"111","5","National Anti-Corruption Strategy Development","Development of a National Anti-Corruption Strategy and the enactment of the Public Service Performance Management (PSPM) Act 2022",""],[1,"111","5","Public Service Performance Management Act Enactment","Development of a National Anti-Corruption Strategy and the enactment of the Public Service Performance Management (PSPM) Act 2022",""],[1,"112","20","Sub-Investigative Committee for Corruption Detection and Investigation","the establishment of a sub investigative committee composed only of agencies responsible for detecting and investigating corruption issues.",""],[1,"113","2","Whistleblower Protection Legal Provisions","Whistleblower protections: legal provisions that encourage reporting of misconduct without fear of retaliation.",""],[1,"119","1","Whistleblower Protection and Anti-Corruption Enforcement Reform","The Government must strengthen existing mechanisms that regulate corrupt practices of leader(s) and public servants to ensure accountability and transparency.",""],[1,"121","1","Good Governance Advocacy and Anti-Corruption Awareness Programmes","Good governance advocacy, through awareness programs focusing on negative impacts of corruption, promoting ethical standards and good governance principles are key factors that could contribute to changing the mindset of the people towards integrity and anti-corruption.",""],[1,"121","3","Civic Education on Corruption and Good Governance","Educating our next generation through formal education about the effects of corruption and good governance will help to create future leaders who will be plagued by the values of good governance and despise the persistence of corruption.",""]],"6":[[1,"6","13","Revenue Collection Strengthening and Improvement","Strengthen and improve the collection of existing revenue sources.",""],[1,"6","14","Sovereign Wealth Fund Management Enhancement","Enhance the management of the Sovereign Wealth Fund known as the Reserve Equalization Reserve Fund (RERF).",""],[1,"6","18","Financial Instruments Access and Aid Coordination Strengthening","Strengthen access to financial instruments and improve aid coordination.",""],[1,"20","4","Revenue Equalization Reserve Fund","To mitigate this risk, the government established the Revenue Equalization Reserve Fund (RERF), a sovereign wealth fund with a strict withdrawal policy designed to ensure long-term sustainability.",""],[1,"29","1","Integration of Planning and Budgeting within NEPO","Integrating planning and budgeting within NEPO is a strategic step that can provide several advantages.",""],[1,"29","11","Medium-Term Fiscal Framework","The Medium-Term Fiscal Framework (MTFF) in Kiribati is an essential tool for managing the country's finances in a sustainable and strategic way.",""],[1,"64","8","Integrated Financial Management Information System (IFMIS)","Improve efficiency and oversight in government financial operations with the new Integrated Financial Management Information System (IFMIS).",""],[1,"64","9","Fiscal Reform and Management Strengthening","ii. Strengthen fiscal reforms and management.",""],[1,"64","12","RERF Management Monitoring and Updating","Continuously maintaining and updating management of the RERF through regular monitoring of the RERF's asset performance and managers.",""],[1,"66","6","Digital Tax Compliance and E-Tax Filing System","Improving compliance through digital tools like e-tax systems to streamline filing and payment process",""],[1,"66","8","Income Tax Act 2023 Implementation and Public Awareness Campaigns","Expanding coverage by introducing the new Income Tax Act 2023 along with public awareness campaigns.",""],[1,"66","10","SOE Financial Position Improvement Measure","A solution to this is to improve the financial position of SOEs, thus increasing payments of SOE dividends and decreasing their dependence on CSOs.",""],[1,"66","15","State-Owned Enterprises Dividend Policy","Developing and implementing a dividend policy to ensure compliance with SOEs.",""],[1,"99","20","Climate Finance Mobilization and Utilization","Securing and effectively utilizing climate finance from",""],[1,"102","10","National Climate Finance Strategy","Develop a national climate finance strategy: Kiribati has launched its National Climate Financing Strategy (KNCFS) to enhance its ability to access and mobilize international climate finance for adaptation and mitigation projects.",""],[1,"147","44","Revenue Collection Strengthening and Improvement","Strengthen and improve the collection of existing revenue sources.",""],[1,"147","50","Sovereign Wealth Fund Management Enhancement","Enhance the management of the Sovereign Wealth Fund (RERF).",""]],"7":[[1,"7","3","Multi-Sectoral NCD Partnership Strengthening","Strengthen partnerships through a multi-sectoral approach to address non-communicable diseases (NCDs).",""],[1,"7","4","NCD Risk Factor Reduction Initiatives","Enhance initiatives and create an enabling environment to tackle NCD risk factors.",""],[1,"7","11","Violence-Free Healthy Lifestyle Promotion","Promote a violence-free, healthy lifestyle among women, youth, and people with disabilities.",""],[1,"7","14","Preventative Mental Health and Suicide Prevention Programs","Implement preventative programs for mental health, accidents, and suicide prevention.",""],[1,"77","27","Community Awareness and Behavioral Change Partnerships","To address these issues, an emphasis on behavioral change through partnerships and community awareness programs is essential.",""],[1,"77","27","Expanded Access to Mental Health Services","Improved access to mental health services programs is required to support the population and address suicide rates.",""],[1,"82","6","Community-Level Public Sport Facilities Expansion","this objective aims to significantly increase the number of new or upgraded community-level public sport facilities completed annually to provide accessible venues for physical activity.",""],[1,"82","7","Community Sports and Physical Activity Participation Initiative","Concurrently, a core focus will be to maximize community engagement, targeting an increase in the number of individuals participating in organized community sports and physical activity fostering widespread and behavioral change through active participation.",""],[1,"89","1","Mental Health Prevention and Support Programme","To strengthen mental health and wellbeing across Kiribati, a range of preventative programs will be implemented.",""],[1,"148","27","Multi-Sectoral Non-Communicable Disease Partnership Strengthening","Strengthen partnerships through a multi- sectoral approach to address non- communicable diseases (NCDs).",""]],"8":[[1,"7","9","Workforce Planning, Development, and Retention Strategy","7. Enhance workforce planning, development, and retention strategies.",""],[1,"7","10","Healthcare Facilities Construction, Maintenance, and Upgrading","Support the construction of new healthcare facilities and the maintenance and upgrading of existing ones.",""],[1,"7","12","Healthcare Services Expansion and New Service Introduction","Support the expansion of existing healthcare services and the introduction of new ones.",""],[1,"74","2","MWYSSA Complementary Health and Social Support Interventions","MWYSSA's related interventions, notably in the areas of Gender-Based Violence (GBV), mental health, social wellbeing, and youth development, complement and support the health outcomes of this KPA.","MWYSSA"],[1,"79","1","Health Sector Strategic Activities Implementation","This strategic priority comprises six strategic objectives that MHMS will achieve through implementation of 10 strategic activities.","MHMS"],[1,"79","1","Health Care Governance and Accountability Strengthening","The strategic objectives focus on strengthening leadership capacity, governance structures, and accountability mechanisms for improved health care services",""],[1,"79","1","Health Care Financing Mechanism Reform","The strategic objectives focus on sustainable health care financing mechanisms to ensure equitable access",""],[1,"79","1","Health Service Delivery Partnership Expansion","The strategic objectives focus on partnerships to complement and support health care service delivery",""],[1,"79","1","Health Workforce Development and Distribution","The strategic objectives focus on a skilled and well-distributed health care workforce",""],[1,"79","1","Health Infrastructure and Asset Management Improvement","The strategic objectives focus on infrastructure and asset management for improved efficiency and safety",""],[1,"79","1","Medical Products Access and Availability Systems","The strategic objectives focus on systems to improve accessibility, availability and medical products.",""],[1,"81","2","Expansion of Healthcare Facilities","Following on from the KDP 2020-2023, ensuring equitable access to healthcare services remains a key priority for MHMS with the ongoing expansion of healthcare facilities to improve access both in terms of the number of healthcare facilities as well as available services.","MHMS"],[1,"81","4","Equitable Access to Specialized Medical Services","The strategic objectives focus on implementing robust health infrastructure for data processes to inform decision-making, improving equitable access to specialized medical services within and outside Kiribati, and reducing the incidence of antimicrobial resistance infections.",""],[1,"149","13","Workforce Planning, Development, and Retention Strategy","Enhance workforce planning, development, and retention strategies",""],[1,"149","22","Health Facility Construction, Maintenance, and Upgrade Programme","Support the construction of new health facilities and maintenance and upgrade of existing health ones.",""]],"9":[[1,"151","10","Improved Enforcement and Prosecution of Environmental Cases","Improved enforcement and prosecution of environment cases to minimize environmental pollution and degradation activities",""],[1,"151","17","Environmental Compliance Improvement for Development Projects","Improve the compliance of development to meet the acceptable environmentally practises and conditions in line with EIA and ESMP to prevent, minimize and mitigate potential environmental impacts and ensuring sustainable",""]],"10":[[1,"8","1","Ecosystem Protection, Conservation, and Restoration Programme","Strengthen, improve and enhancing the protection, conservation, sustainable management, and restoration of ecosystems and natural resources, while strengthening their resilience and adaptive capacities to climate change, environmental degradation and other environmental stressors.",""],[1,"93","6","National Protected Area Patrolling Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening national patrolling capacity to improve the monitoring of the protected areas through provision of patrolling equipment and training conducted to staff funded by EU and ACP Group and implemented by BIOPAMA.",""],[1,"93","7","Protected Areas Management Plan Development","Improving the protection of biodiversity through the development of the protected areas management plan including the Integrated Environment Natural Resources Co-Management Plan (IENRP) which provide directions and proper approaches on how resources will be conserved in a particular area or community groups (funded by FAO and EU and ACP group supports).",""],[1,"94","1","Environmental and Biodiversity Awareness Programs","Improving awareness on the importance of protecting the environment and biodiversity through conduction of ongoing awareness programs targeting all the stakeholders focusing on demonstrating the importance of protecting ecosystems and habitats and promoting proper environmental approaches.",""],[1,"96","3","Carbon Sequestration Monitoring and Assessment Mechanism","Efforts have also been made to develop mechanisms for monitoring and assessing carbon sequestration through terrestrial and coastal ecosystems.",""],[1,"103","4","Environmental Monitoring and Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthening of environmental monitoring and enforcement to promote compliance with sustainable development practices in line with the Environment Licensing (EO) requirements, ESMP and the EIA requirements.",""],[1,"103","4","Endangered Species and Community Resource Management Plans","Promoting management and conservation of resources include endangered species through development and implementation of management plans, development and implementation of IENRPs by the respective communities, ongoing awareness programs and other conservation activities are also critical areas that need to be enhanced.",""],[1,"150","28","Coastal Protection and Biodiversity Conservation through Mangrove Planting","Improved coastal protection and the protection of biodiversity at vulnerable areas through mangrove plantation, constructuion of coastal brush and conservation of resources",""]],"11":[[1,"8","4","Cultural Mapping for Heritage Data Improvement","Strengthen and improve data and information on historical and cultural heritages through Cultural Mapping in Kiribati.",""],[1,"8","5","Cultural and Historical Site Protection from Climate Impacts","Protecting and Preserving Cultural and Historical sites and War Relics from Climate Change Impacts, as well as other development and social activities. through collaboration with stakeholders and incentives for site owners",""],[1,"8","6","Traditional Knowledge and Skills Preservation Collaboration","Protecting and preserving traditional knowledge and skill through collaboration with knowledge and skills holders and the local communities.",""],[1,"95","8","Island Cultural Documentation and Safeguarding","the work on such is continuous, trying to ensure that islands in Kiribati are visited, and that each island's unique stories and traditional skills as well as diverse Cultural Values are documented and safeguarded.",""],[1,"95","8","Youth Training in Traditional Skills","Other works including training of youths on traditional skills remains part of the office's routine work to support the sustainable development of our cultural heritage and maintaining the identify of an I-Kiribati.",""],[1,"105","3","Cultural Mapping and Heritage Documentation Programme","Cultural Mapping is a vital strategy for strengthening data and documentation on Kiribati's cultural heritage and historical events, which define the identity of the I-Kiribati people.","Culture & Museum Division (CMD)"],[1,"106","1","Cultural Identity Preservation and Heritage Legacy Programme","The Government of Kiribati recognizes the significance of this program and is committed to its implementation as a priority under this KPA, to preserve cultural identity, inform policy, and sustain the Kiribati's cultural legacy.",""],[1,"106","3","Cultural Heritage Partnership and Community Collaboration Initiative","MCIA recognizes that much work is needed on seeking meaningful support and to create a durable partnership at the national and international level to complement the government's assistance and support to this area.","MCIA"],[1,"106","3","Community-Based Cultural Heritage Participation Approach","Strengthening our partnership and collaboration with the communities, who are the custodians of our cultural heritage, is vital as they are the resources and the protectors of all that matter in this area.","MCIA"],[1,"106","4","Traditional Knowledge and Skills Documentation and Preservation","The collection and documentation of human wealth or resources, such as traditional knowledge and skills, will benefit both the current and future generations.",""],[1,"106","5","Public Education Campaign for Traditional Knowledge Sharing","Public education to influence behaviour, so that knowledge and skills sharing can be done voluntarily is needed to create an enabling environment and gain the support of local communities, particularly holders of traditional knowledge and skills.",""],[1,"106","5","Incentive-Based Collaboration for Traditional Knowledge Holders","Following intensive campaigns, collaboration that provides rewards for knowledge and skills holders would help address customary practices that regard resistance to sharing such wealth outside family lines as a wise choice.",""],[1,"106","6","Enabling Institution for Intellectual Property Protection","This will require collaboration between government agencies to establish a proper enabling institution so that knowledge and skills holders can willingly cooperate and share their resources.",""],[1,"107","1","Public Education on Traditional Knowledge and Skills","public education on the importance of sharing traditional knowledge and skills",""],[1,"107","1","Stakeholder Collaboration on Traditional Knowledge and Skills","collaboration between the CMD of the MCIA and relevant stakeholders, including holders of traditional knowledge and skills",""],[1,"107","3","National Cultural Values Study","To safeguard this heritage, a full-scale study of cultural values across Kiribati is essential.",""],[1,"107","4","Technical and Financial Support for CMD Survey and Documentation Work","Successful implementation depends on technical and financial support, particularly for the CMD to lead surveys and documentation efforts.",""],[1,"107","4","CSO and Community Collaboration for Cultural Value Promotion","Equally important is strong collaboration with CSOs, especially churches, local communities, and Island Councils, whose grassroots leadership is vital for promoting, transmitting, and sustaining cultural values.",""],[1,"152","3","Cultural Mapping for Heritage Data and Information","Strengthen and improve data and information about historical and cultural heritages through Cultural Mapping in Kiribati",""],[1,"152","6","Cultural and Historical Site Protection and Preservation Initiative","Protecting and Preserving Cultural and Historical sites and War Relics from Climate Change Impacts and other development and social activities through collaboration with stakeholders and incentives for site owners",""]],"12":[[1,"8","17","Safe Drinking Water and Sanitation Provision","Ensure safe drinking water sources and proper sanitation.",""],[1,"127","4","Household Water Tank Distribution and Rural Water Reticulation Expansion","Almost 12,000 water tanks were distributed to individual households, mainly in South Tarawa and some Outer Islands as well as the expansion of water reticulation systems to ensure that all households in rural areas have access to a reliable water supply.","Water and Sanitation Engineering Department (WSED) of MISE"],[1,"127","4","Outer Islands Water Tank Funding Mobilization","dialogue was initiated to secure funds for distribution of water tanks to individual households in all the Outer Islands.",""],[1,"127","4","Solar Pump and Desalination System Deployment","Forty solar pumps and 7 desalination plants were installed, whereas, till 2023, Kiribati has ensured a total 14,125 sanitation facilities.",""],[1,"127","4","Water System Rehabilitation and Replacement Fund","through regular Maintenance Fund and Disaster Resilience Fund, the Government have procured new solar powered desalination systems and rehabilitated/replaced dis-functional water systems in selected Outer Islands.",""],[1,"127","4","Water Services Rehabilitation under the Water Scarcity Project","The Water Scarcity Project also provided support for rehabilitating these water services.",""],[1,"127","4","South Tarawa Water Supply Project","MISE launched the South Tarawa Water Supply Project, funded by ADB, WB, Green Climate Fund, Global Environment Fund (GEF) and GoK, aiming to provide sustainable water supply to South Tarawa and Betio through the construction of two desalination plants (Betio and Mckenzie Desal Plants) and then get piped water provided by the Public Utilities Board (PUB).","MISE"],[1,"128","5","Outer Islands Water Challenge Response Initiatives","To address the ongoing water challenges in the Outer Islands, the Kiribati government continues to implement strategic initiatives and allocate funding in collaboration with development partners through the following initiatives:",""],[1,"129","1","Outer Islands Water Scarcity Response Initiatives","These initiatives are either initiated or underway to address challenges on water scarcity in the Outer Islands.",""],[1,"129","1","South Tarawa Sanitation Project","The South Tarawa Sanitation Project, funded by WB and GoK also launched, aiming to increase access to sewer networks for Betio, Bairiki and Bikenibeu as well as installation of onsite sanitation systems on a number of villages on South Tarawa.",""],[1,"129","1","Bonriki Water Reserve Monitoring","The monitoring of the Bonriki Water Reserve was carried out regularly.",""],[1,"129","1","Water Supply and Sanitation Financing Mobilization","MISE carried out dialogues with multiple development partners to secure funds to accelerate the delivery of water supply and sanitation services.","MISE"],[1,"134","6","Feasibility Study for Drilling New Water Resources in Outer Islands","Conducting the feasibility of drilling new water resources in the outer islands",""],[1,"135","13","Safe Drinking Water Access Expansion Initiative","Under the new KDP, key initiatives are underway to expand access to safe drinking water across both rural and urban areas.",""],[1,"135","13","Rural Rainwater Harvesting Tank Distribution","In rural Kiribati, the government will distribute 3,000-liter water tanks to improve rainwater harvesting.",""],[1,"135","13","Urban Water Tank Distribution for New Leases","Meanwhile in urban areas - particularly for new leases - the Ministry of Line and Phoenix Islands Development (MLPID) will distribute 800 water tanks of 500-liter capacity.","Ministry of Line and Phoenix Islands Development (MLPID)"],[1,"135","14","Expansion of Piped Water Access","the government is prioritizing the expansion of piped water access.",""],[1,"135","15","South Tarawa Water Supply Project","the South Tarawa Water Supply Project (STWSP), implemented by PUB, an SOE- launched in 2020 and running through 2029-is scaling up desalinated water production",""],[1,"136","1","Desalination Unit Rehabilitation and Replacement Programme","Outside South Tarawa, non-functioning desalination units will be rehabilitated or replaced.",""],[1,"136","1","Outer Island Desalination Plant Installation Programme","New plants will also be installed in selected outer island communities by MISE or with its technical support, with funding from partners including SPC and MFAT.","MISE"],[1,"136","2","Deployment of Portable Solar Desalination Units","Under MISE's coordination, these units will be deployed to water-scarce and drought-affected communities, or where permanent plants are not operational, as an immediate relief measure.","MISE"],[1,"136","3","Sustainable Financing for Desalination System Operations and Maintenance","MISE in collaboration with its key stakeholders are actively engaging with development partners to secure sustainable financing to ensure long-term functionality of these essential services across both South Tarawa and the Outer Islands.","MISE"],[1,"136","6","South Tarawa Sanitation Project","To address these challenges, the South Tarawa Sanitation Project (STSP), was implemented.",""],[1,"136","7","Communal and Public Toilet Construction Programme","The STSP also plans to construct 30 communal toilets and 44 public toilets throughout South Tarawa.",""],[1,"136","8","Sanitation Program Extension to Outer Islands and Remote Groups","MISE is currently in discussions with development partners to mobilize financial support for the extension of sanitation programs to these more remote and underserved communities.","MISE | MLPID"]],"13":[[1,"129","1","National WASH Coordination and Committee Meetings","MISE through WSED took a lead role for organizing Kiribati National Steering Committee meetings, Kiribati WASH Coordination Committee meetings, Kiribati National Drought Committee meetings and Kiribati National Water Quality Monitoring Committee meetings.","MISE | WSED"]],"14":[[1,"130","2","Airport Facilities Improvement Works","Improvement works at Bonriki and Kiritimati international airport facilities are ongoing, in alignment with the requirements of international aviation standards.",""],[1,"130","2","Cassidy International Airport Maintenance and Rehabilitation","maintenance and rehabilitation work for Cassidy International Airport are scheduled to begin in 2025, with funding support from the WB.",""],[1,"130","2","Airport Masterplan Development","The development of the airport masterplan, covering Bonriki International Airport and related infrastructure is also being progressed, with support from the Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade (DFAT), and is on track for completion by end of 2025.",""],[1,"130","2","Outer Islands Airport Infrastructure Upgrading and Maintenance","the upgrading and maintenance of airport infrastructure across the outer islands has reached approximately 40% completion.",""],[1,"130","2","Inter-Island Air Transport Service Strengthening","To support improved connectivity, inter-island air transport services have also been strengthened, marked by an increase in the number of operational aircraft under AKL.",""],[1,"130","2","Additional Aircraft Acquisition","Plans are in place to acquire an additional aircraft, increasing the fleet from four to five.",""],[1,"140","2","Embraer Jet Investment for International Flights","Kiribati's two Embraer Jets which soon commence international flights.",""],[1,"140","3","Cassidy International Airport Upgrading Works","Additionally, more upgrading works on Cassidy International airport will commence in late 2025 or in 2026.",""],[1,"140","5","Outer Island Airport Runway Remediation Project","there is an on-going runway remediation project that has been carried out in the Outer Island to minimize the risk of accidents and ensure smooth operation",""],[1,"140","6","Airport Rehabilitation and Construction Programme","There are plans to rehabilitate the existing airport in Kanton and construct a new airport in Banaba.",""],[1,"140","7","Airport Upgrade Investment Programme","Investing in the upgrade of these airports to meet a standard design requirement will significantly enhance air services and more importantly, improve the safety of our nationals.",""],[1,"142","4","Airport Construction and Upgrade Investment","investments in international and domestic airport construction and upgrades will ensure that facilities meet required standards and improve overall transportation efficiency.",""],[1,"142","5","Airport Development and Modernization Programme","The development and modernization of international and domestic airports will ensure compliance with required standards, leading to more efficient and reliable transportation services.",""],[1,"155","23","Airport Construction and Upgrading Programme","Increase in number of airports and its facilities constructured and upgraded to meet the international standard",""]],"15":[[1,"126","3","National Infrastructure Investment Plan","the Government has formulated and launched the National Infrastructure Investment Plan (NIIP) 2023-2033 to comprehensively assess infrastructure needs across all sectors at the national level.",""],[1,"126","3","Maintenance Policy Development","the Maintenance Policy is currently under development, aiming to provide guiding frameworks to ensure the efficient utilization of the maintenance fund and to ensure that the government's major assets were sustained.",""],[1,"137","3","Building Code and Standards Enforcement","Enforcement and implementation of the Kiribati Building Act 2024 and Kiribati Building Code 2024 is the next targeted move within this new KDP 2024-2027 period.",""],[1,"137","4","Resilient Building Design Standards","Designing buildings to be resilient against climate change and extreme weather events is essential.",""],[1,"137","5","Government Buildings Regular Maintenance and Inspection Programme","Regular Maintenance: Ongoing maintenance and inspections to the government buildings are vital to ensure longevity and safety of buildings.",""],[1,"137","7","Building and Occupancy Approval Issuance and Code Enforcement","MISE is solely responsible for the issuance of building and occupancy approvals, whilst the Ministry of Line and Phoenix Islands Development (MLPID) assist with the enforcement of conformance to the building Code Act for the issuance of building approvals only to normal and basic building infrastructures that are carried out in the Line and Phoenix Islands Development.","MISE | Ministry of Line and Phoenix Islands Development (MLPID)"]],"16":[[1,"5","14","Student Enrollment Support","Facilitate and assist student enrolment at all grade levels.",""],[1,"5","17","Inclusive Education Support for Students with Special Needs","Identify students with special needs and ensure they have access to education in mainstream schools.",""],[1,"32","4","Free and Compulsory Education Expansion","Key initiatives include the implementation of free and compulsory education from primary to secondary levels (Years 1-12), the provision of partial subsidies for eligible Year 13 students, and the expansion of scholarships for higher education.",""],[1,"32","4","Higher Education Scholarship Expansion","Key initiatives include the implementation of free and compulsory education from primary to secondary levels (Years 1-12), the provision of partial subsidies for eligible Year 13 students, and the expansion of scholarships for higher education.",""],[1,"43","27","Education Service Quality Improvement","this phase of implementation will concentrate on tackling the key challenges identified and enhancing the quality of education services and delivery.",""],[1,"43","27","Cross-Ministry Education Strategy Alignment and Coordination","The strategies outlined are drawn from the sector plans of key ministries, including the MoE, Ministry of Women, Youth, Sport and Social Affairs (MWYSSA), the MEHR, KPS and the MHMS are directly aligned with the strategic priorities of the KDP.","MoE | Ministry of Women, Youth, Sport and Social Affairs (MWYSSA) | MEHR | KPS | MHMS"],[1,"43","27","Coordinated Education Access and Participation Improvement","This alignment ensures that government efforts remain well-coordinated and mutually reinforcing, resulting in improved access and participation, stronger student outcomes, greater inclusivity, expanded training pathways, and more effective public service delivery.",""],[1,"44","3","School Construction and Renovation with WASH Facilities","Construct and renovate schools, including Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) facilities, in accordance with National Infrastructure Standards (NIS) and building codes.",""],[1,"44","4","Re-entry Pathways into Formal Education and Training","Facilitate re-entry pathways into formal education and training for those who have dropped out.",""],[1,"44","5","Student Transportation Improvement for Remote and Outer Island Communities","Improve student transportation, particularly for children in remote and outer island communities.",""],[1,"44","6","Expansion of Model Inclusion Schools and Upgrade of Islet Primary Schools","Expand the coverage of Model Inclusion Schools and upgrade islet primary schools to offer JSS education.",""],[1,"44","7","Free Meal Program","Address financial barriers to access by introducing a Free Meal Program.",""],[1,"44","8","Free and Compulsory Education Policy Enforcement","Strengthen enforcement of the Free and Compulsory Education Policy.",""],[1,"44","9","Stakeholder and Development Partner Coordination for Education Initiatives","Enhance collaboration with national stakeholders and development partners to support and sustain education initiatives.",""],[1,"44","10","No-Quota Scholarship Scheme Expansion","Introduce and expand no-quota scholarship scheme to ensure that all students who meet the minimum passing grade can access further education without being limited by scholarship quotas.",""],[1,"45","1","Student Assessment and Teacher Quality Strengthening","Keyways that the MoE will adopt to enhance student performance is by strengthening assessment frameworks to track progress, enhanced teacher quality, identify learning gaps, and guide targeted interventions and promote an inclusive and violent free environment in Kiribati.","MoE"],[1,"45","1","Targeted Learning Support and Inclusive School Environment","Keyways that the MoE will adopt to enhance student performance is by strengthening assessment frameworks to track progress, enhanced teacher quality, identify learning gaps, and guide targeted interventions and promote an inclusive and violent free environment in Kiribati.","MoE"],[1,"45","3","School Internet Access Expansion","Expand internet access to Junior and Secondary School Schools and to Primary School head teachers",""],[1,"46","3","Provision of Quality Teaching and Learning Resources to Schools","Provide all schools with quality teaching and learning resources",""],[1,"46","4","Inclusive Teaching Materials and Assistive Learning Tools for Schools","This strategy focuses on equipping all schools with inclusive teaching materials and assistive learning tools to support students with diverse learning needs.",""],[1,"46","5","Expand Model Inclusion Schools and Extend Islet Primary Schools to JSS","Expand Model Inclusion Schools and extend islet primary schools to JSS",""],[1,"46","6","Model Inclusion Schools Expansion","The number of Model Inclusion Schools will be increased, and inclusive education will be extended from primary to Junior Secondary School (JSS), with a particular focus on the outer islands.",""],[1,"46","6","Teacher Aide Recruitment for Special Needs Support","Additional teacher aides will be recruited to support students with special needs in these schools.",""],[1,"47","2","Early Identification and Support for Students with Special Needs","Kiribati is committed to ensuring that students with special needs are identified early and provided with the necessary support to excel in mainstream schools.",""],[1,"47","6","School-Community Partnership Strengthening","Strengthen partnerships with families, communities and institutions to support student goals.",""],[1,"145","4","Student Enrollment Support","Facilitate and assist student enrolment at all grade levels",""],[1,"146","4","Inclusive Education Access for Students with Special Needs","Identify students with special needs and ensure they have access to education in mainstream schools",""]],"17":[[1,"5","18","Accessible Formal and Informal Training Pathways","Strengthen and provide pathways for accessible formal and informal training opportunities.",""],[1,"32","2","Innovative Education Access and Connectivity Investments","In response to the challenges and opportunities of a rapidly evolving global landscape, strategic investments in education, public service, and vocational training are crucial to cultivating a skilled and resilient workforce.",""],[1,"38","10","Workforce Skills Gap Analysis and Training Improvement Initiative","Looking ahead, the PSO aims to refine workforce skills gap analysis, enhance training effectiveness, and expand collaborations with donors.",""],[1,"39","2","TVET Enrolment Expansion at KIT and MTC","The aim is to increase enrolment to address the needs of school leavers.",""],[1,"40","2","Sector-Specific Frontline Services Training Investment","The Government continues to invest in sector-specific training to strengthen critical frontline services.",""],[1,"40","2","Kiribati Student of Nursing Transfer to MHMS","The Kiribati Student of Nursing has now transferred to the Ministry of Health and Medical Services (MHMS), a move intended to better align nursing education with sectoral workforce planning, enhance clinical and simulation-based training, and improve overall program quality.","Ministry of Health and Medical Services (MHMS)"],[1,"46","7","Inclusive TVET Access and Support Services","The Kiribati Institute of Technology (KIT) will ensure equitable access to training by accommodating individuals with disabilities and promoting gender equality in both trade and non-trade programs.",""],[1,"46","8","Community-Based Vocational and Life Skills Training Expansion","The MWYSSA will expand access to vocational and life skills training for disadvantaged groups- including women, youth, and persons with disabilities-through community-driven programs in both urban and outer island areas.","MWYSSA"],[1,"46","9","Decentralized Life Skills Training","Decentralize life skills training to outer islands",""],[1,"46","10","Decentralized Life Skills Training Programme","MWYSSA will decentralize life skills programs by engaging skilled local trainers and partnering with Island Councils.",""],[1,"46","12","Disability-Focused Institutional Collaboration MoUs","Strengthening collaboration with disability-focused institutions through new Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with organizations such as Te Toa Matoa, Kiribati School and Center for Students with Disabilities, Kiribati Association for people who are Blind or Vision Impaired (KABVI), Te Meeria, Kiribati Deaf Association.",""],[1,"46","13","Expanded ICT and Trade Training Programs","Expanding Training and Customized Programs: By offering Certificate 1 in ICT, Trade courses and two full time Kiri Sign Interpreters to assist students with hearing impairments, ensuring full participation in student activities at all school levels.",""],[1,"47","11","Training Systems Strengthening and Expansion","Efforts to enhance and expand training systems across all sectors remain a national priority.",""],[1,"47","12","Targeted Support for Youth Skills Strategy Implementation","the Government is committed to providing targeted support for the implementation of strategies in the following key areas:",""],[1,"47","14","KIT Outer Island Centers Expansion","KIT Outer Island Centers: New centers in Abemama (2018), Kiritimati (2019), and Abaiang (2025) aim to decentralize vocational training.",""],[1,"47","15","Youth Bridging Programs","Youth Bridging Programs: In partnership with Child Fund, KIT offers foundational and employability training to reintegrate early school leavers into learning pathways.",""],[1,"47","16","Short Non-Formal Courses Expansion","KIT has expanded short-term training in areas like aged care, business, and community services, achieving a 58% success rate in the last KDP.",""],[1,"47","17","School of Nursing Re-establishment and Expansion","Support the re-establishment and expansion of the School of Nursing under MHMS, along with increased intake and capacity in police training.","MHMS"],[1,"48","1","Training Facilities Upgrade and Field-Based Learning Enhancement","Infrastructure Improvements: Upgrade training facilities and enhance field-based learning to improve practical competencies.",""],[1,"48","2","Expansion of Program Offerings and New Industry-Aligned Initiatives","The Government, through the relevant Ministries, will continue to expand programs offerings by developing new initiatives that align with industry demands and employment pathways.","relevant Ministries"],[1,"48","3","ECCE Training Program and Simulation Training Space","A new ECCE training program will be launched in 2026, supported by a dedicated simulation training space for early childhood teachers and community educators.",""],[1,"48","4","TVET in Schools Alignment Initiative","TVET in Schools: A collaboration between KIT and the MoE aims to align technical and vocational training with secondary school curricula, allowing students to transition into KIT programs seamlessly.","KIT | MoE"],[1,"48","5","Renewable Energy Training Certificate","Renewable Energy Training: KIT, in partnership with KASfEP, will introduce a Certificate IV in Electrical Renewable Energy in 2026 to address the growing demand for solar and renewable energy expertise.",""],[1,"48","6","Refrigeration and Air Conditioning Training Program","Refrigeration and Air Conditioning (RAC) Program: Supported by UNEP and MELAD, this new program, launching in Term 2 of 2025, will provide specialized training for the installation and maintenance of air conditioning systems.","MELAD"],[1,"48","7","Youth Learning Centre and Life Skills Programs","A new Youth Learning Centre will offer life skills, employability training, and cultural mentorship programs for young people, encouraging personal development and career progression.",""],[1,"48","8","Labor Market Alignment for Training Programs","KIT is enhancing collaboration with the MoE, MELAD, private employers, and development partners to align programs with labor market needs.","MoE | MELAD"],[1,"48","8","Inclusive Vocational Training Partnerships","New MoUs are being formed with disability organizations such as Te Toa Matoa and KSCSD to improve inclusivity in vocational training.",""],[1,"48","9","Maritime Training Programs","MTC continues to offer training under the Interdepartmental Flexibility (IDF), Fishing Vessel Personnel (FVP), and Basic Steward and Hospitality Course (BSHC) programs, preparing I-Kiribati for maritime careers when demand arises.",""],[1,"48","10","Expansion of International Shipping Partnerships","Expanding international shipping partnerships through new MoUs",""],[1,"48","11","Instructor Training Alignment with KIT","Strengthening teaching capacity by aligning MTC instructors with KIT for relevant training support",""],[1,"146","8","Accessible Formal and Informal Training Opportunities","Strengthen and provide pathways for accessible formal and informal training opportunities",""],[1,"146","45","Human Resource Development Systems and Strategies Strengthening","Strengthen and enhance HRD systems/strategies that promote continuous learning and address current and future skill gaps",""]],"18":[[1,"6","15","Overseas Employment Market Retention and Job Opportunity Expansion","Maintain existing overseas employment markets while securing new domestic and international job opportunities.",""],[1,"68","6","Overseas Employment Expansion through Labour Migration Policies","The Government is actively expanding overseas employment opportunities for its citizens through strategic labour migration policies aligned with the KV20 development goals.",""],[1,"68","6","Use of Existing Labour Mobility Programs","It is leveraging existing programs like Observers, Australia's PALM Scheme and New Zealand's RSE program while negotiating new agreements to access emerging sectors with the existing markets.",""],[1,"68","7","Overseas Labour Mobility Worker Quality Enhancement","To revitalize its overseas labour mobility program and address recent declines, the Government will enhance worker quality through.",""],[1,"68","8","Conduct Agreements and Reformed Pre-departure Training","Building conduct agreements and reformed pre-departure training",""],[1,"68","9","Employer Trust-Building Through Performance Reporting and Dispute Resolution","ii. Rebuilding employer trust via transparent performance reporting and/or dispute resolution system.",""],[1,"68","11","Employer-Driven Reforms and Skills Development","Prioritizing employer-driven reforms and skills development, the Government aims to secure its position as a competitive labour-sending nation in the Pacific, which contributed to the reduction of unemployment and alleviate hardship.",""],[1,"146","20","International Maritime Compliance and Maritime Job Creation","International Maritime compliance. Filling job oppourtunities at sea and on land.",""],[1,"148","4","Overseas Employment Market Maintenance and Job Opportunity Expansion","Maintain existing overseas employment markets while securing new domestic and international job oppurtunities.",""]],"19":[[1,"6","16","Targeted Subsidies and Social Protection Measures","Providing targeted subsidies and social protection measures.",""],[1,"53","3","Targeted Social Protection Spending Measures","the Government is firmly committed in adopting targeted spending measures to strengthen social protection initiatives, with the goal of empowering local communities and improving their livelihoods.",""],[1,"69","2","Targeted Spending for Social Protection Mechanisms","the government is firmly committed in adopting targeted spending measures to strengthen new and existing social protection mechanisms to empower local communities and improve their livelihoods.",""],[1,"69","3","Social Protection Program Enhancement","This commitment has led to the introduction and enhancement of existing social protection programs aimed at supporting unemployed individuals, elderly citizens, and people with disabilities, while also helping to narrow the gap of income inequality.",""],[1,"69","4","Copra Subsidy for Outer Islands Households","To reduce rural-to-urban migration, the government provides a copra subsidy to support individuals residing in the Outer Islands.",""],[1,"69","6","Social Assistance for Vulnerable Groups","Among the financial support offered by the government are social provisions for vulnerable groups, including people with disabilities and senior citizens aged 70 and above.",""],[1,"69","6","Support for Registered Churches","the government also provides support to registered churches to accommodate their operational needs and better serve their congregations.",""],[1,"71","4","Essential Services and Hardship Alleviation Programme","while continuing to deliver essential services and hardship alleviation programs.",""],[1,"148","13","Targeted Subsidies and Social Protection Measures","Providing targeted subsidies and social protection measures",""],[1,"148","19","Expanded Access to Tobwaan te Rikirake Loan Scheme for Marginalized Groups","Increase the number of marginalized groups access to Tobwaan te Rikirake loan scheme",""]],"20":[[1,"7","5","Targeted Communicable Disease Prevention, Detection, and Management","Improve the prevention, detection, and management of targeted communicable diseases (CDs).",""],[1,"7","6","Targeted Neglected Tropical Diseases Prevention, Detection, and Management","Strengthen the prevention, detection, and management of targeted neglected tropical diseases (NTDs).",""],[1,"74","2","National Health Strategic Plan 2024-2027","This plan outlines six strategic priorities to catalyze change in the health system and health of people in Kiribati related to: leadership and governance; health systems; promoting healthy lifestyles and reducing preventable morbidity, mortality and disability related to NCDs, CDs and mental health, family-orientated health strategies; and health protection and preparedness to address environmental health issues, outbreaks, emergencies and climate resilience.","MHMS"],[1,"78","8","Community Awareness and Behavioral Change Programs","Innovative approaches must be adopted whilst maintaining continued focus on community awareness programs and behavioral change incentives.",""],[1,"78","8","Cross-Sector Health Partnerships","Creative partnerships within and beyond the healthcare sector to tackle complex health challenges and achieve national health and development goals.",""],[1,"78","8","Health System Strengthening for Better Outcomes","Through collaborative efforts and a focus on the six strategic priorities, Kiribati aims to enhance the health and well-being of its citizens, ensuring better health outcomes for all, regardless of geographic location.",""],[1,"81","4","Antimicrobial Resistance Reduction Measures","The strategic objectives focus on implementing robust health infrastructure for data processes to inform decision-making, improving equitable access to specialized medical services within and outside Kiribati, and reducing the incidence of antimicrobial resistance infections.",""],[1,"83","5","Communicable Disease Control Strategic Activities","This strategic priority comprises four strategic objectives that MHMS will achieve through implementation of four strategic activities.","MHMS"],[1,"84","2","National Vaccination Coverage Expansion","maintaining or increasing national vaccination coverage above WHO recommended targets",""],[1,"148","38","Targeted Communicable Disease Prevention, Detection, and Management","Improve prevention, detection, and management of targeted communicable diseases (CDs).",""]],"21":[[1,"7","7","Maternal and Newborn Care Improvement","5. Improve the availability, accessibility, and quality of maternal and newborn care during pregnancy, delivery, and the postpartum period.",""],[1,"149","3","Maternal and Newborn Care Service Improvement","Improve the availability, accessibility, and quality of services and quality of maternal and newborn care during pregnancy, delivery, and the postpartum period",""],[1,"149","10","Child Malnutrition Reduction Measures","Reduce the burden of child malnutrition by addressing comorbidities, promoting exclusive breasfeeding, and ensuring appropriate complementary feeding.",""]],"22":[[1,"7","13","Gender-Based Violence Prevention and Response Mechanisms","Strengthen mechanisms for preventing and responding to gender-based violence (GBV).",""],[1,"84","2","Standardized SGBV Care Services in Health Facilities","improving access to standardized care and services for sexual and gender-based violence (SGBV) in all healthcare facilities",""],[1,"88","4","Young Couple Program Expansion","The Young Couple Program, implemented by the MWYSSA since July 2018, will be expanded to reach a greater number of young couples aged 21 to 35 years.","MWYSSA"],[1,"88","5","Positive Parenting Program","a Positive Parenting Program will be developed and implemented to promote safe and nurturing family environments",""],[1,"88","5","GBV Coordination Strengthening","National efforts will also focus on strengthening coordination among law enforcement agencies, medical professionals, and social service providers to ensure a comprehensive and survivor-centered response to GBV",""],[1,"88","5","GBV Public Awareness Campaigns","Public awareness campaigns will be intensified to raise community understanding of GBV, its impacts, and the support services available",""],[1,"88","6","Expansion of the Kiribati Men's Behavioral Program","The Kiribati Men's Behavioral Program will be expanded to the outer islands to provide more opportunities for men to transform harmful attitudes and behaviors, while encouraging their active participation in advocacy and awareness initiatives aimed at ending violence against women and girls.",""],[1,"88","6","Strengthening of the SafeNet Initiative","Furthermore, the SafeNet initiative will be strengthened through enhanced coordination with partners to support the seamless implementation of GBV programs.",""],[1,"88","6","GBV Training and Community Awareness Expansion","Training and awareness activities will be expanded to cover critical topics including gender dynamics, referral pathways, types and cycles of violence, and best practices in prevention and response, thereby building stronger community-based mechanisms to combat GBV across Kiribati.",""],[1,"149","26","Domestic Violence Reduction Initiatives","Empowering youth, young couples and family units through initiatives targeted at reducing domestic violence against women.",""],[1,"149","27","Domestic Violence Prevention and Reduction Measures","Control and reduce forms of domestic violence against women.",""],[1,"149","31","Gender-Based Violence Prevention and Response Mechanisms","Strengthen mechanisms for preventing and responding to gender-based violence (GBV)",""],[1,"149","39","Counselling Services Expansion","Increase number of couselling services provide",""]],"23":[[1,"7","16","Environmental Resilience Building through the KDP and Associated Policies","Through the KDP and associated policies (e.g., KIEP, KJIP), and with support from all levels, Kiribati will build a strong foundation for environmental resilience.",""],[1,"7","18","Atoll Vulnerability Reduction and Environmental Resilience Programme","Focus on removing, reducing, and managing the atoll vulnerabilities and local environmental threats, and building and enhancing key drivers for environmental resilience to minimize current and future impact associated with climate change, natural and human - induced hazards, and disaster risks.",""],[1,"25","3","Resilience-Oriented Investment Prioritization","Moving forward, greater emphasis must be placed on investments that enhance resilience, particularly in areas like renewable energy, sustainable fisheries, and climate-adaptive infrastructure.",""],[1,"96","3","National Adaptation and Disaster Risk Capacity-Building Measures","Other key achievements include the development of a national adaptation plan, conducting disaster simulation exercises at school level, building humanitarian warehouse, community awareness raising and campaigns, training and capacity building programs to bolster national and local capacity to manage climate and disaster risks.",""],[1,"101","6","Institutional Capacity Building for Climate Adaptation and Disaster Risk Management","Provide training and resources to government agencies at national level to effectively plan, implement, and monitor climate change adaptation and DRM strategies.",""],[1,"101","7","Inter-Ministerial Coordination for Climate Action and Risk Reduction","Improve inter-ministerial coordination: Foster better communication and collaboration between different government ministries (e.g., environment, infrastructure, finance, health) to ensure a cohesive and integrated approach to climate action and risk reduction.",""],[1,"101","8","Climate and Disaster Risk Mainstreaming in Planning and Budgeting","Mainstream climate and disaster risk into national planning and budgeting: Ensure that climate change and disaster risks are explicitly considered and integrated into all national and sectoral policies, development plans, and budget allocations.",""],[1,"101","9","Legal and Policy Framework Review for Environmental Protection and Disaster Risk Reduction","Strengthen legal and policy frameworks: Review and update existing legislation related to environmental protection, disaster management, and land-use planning to create an enabling environment for effective adaptation and risk reduction measures.",""],[1,"101","10","Community Participation Mechanisms for Adaptation and Disaster Risk Management","Establish mechanisms for local communities, including vulnerable groups, to actively participate in the planning, decision-making, and implementation of adaptation and DRM initiatives.",""],[1,"101","12","Multi-Hazard Early Warning Systems Strengthening","Develop and strengthen early warning systems: Invest in and improve the accuracy and effectiveness of an end-to-end multi hazard early warning systems.",""],[1,"101","13","Disaster Preparedness Drills and Training Programme","Conduct regular disaster preparedness drills and training for government agencies, first responders, communities, and vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"101","13","Disaster Response Resource Provision","Ensure that adequate resources, including equipment and supplies, are in place for effective response and relief efforts.",""],[1,"102","1","Community-Based Disaster Preparedness and Response Planning","This includes supporting the development of community-based disaster preparedness and response plans and providing training in first aid, search and rescue, and evacuation procedures.",""],[1,"102","2","Risk and Vulnerability Assessment and Hazard Mapping","Improve risk and vulnerability assessment and mapping: Conduct comprehensive risk assessments to identify areas and populations that are vulnerable and are at risk for primary hazards such as drought and sea level rise.",""],[1,"102","2","Hazard Risk Mapping for Planning and Preparedness","Develop hazard risk maps to inform land-use planning, infrastructure development, and emergency preparedness efforts.",""],[1,"102","3","Risk Transfer Mechanism Feasibility Study","Explore risk transfer mechanisms: Investigate the feasibility of risk transfer mechanisms, such as insurance, to help the government and communities manage the financial impacts of disasters.",""],[1,"102","5","Climate Change and Disaster Risk Management Education and Awareness Program","Develop and implement education and awareness programs on climate change impacts, adaptation strategies, and DRM for all levels of society, from schools to the public.",""],[1,"102","6","Integration of Traditional Knowledge into Adaptation and Disaster Risk Management","Recognize and integrate traditional knowledge and practices related to weather forecasting, natural resource management, and disaster preparedness into adaptation and DRM strategies.",""],[1,"102","7","Specialized Technical Training for Local Communities","Provide specialized training to local communities and populations such as climate science, disaster and climate risk assessment, coastal and electrical engineering, construction, plumbing, and environmental management.",""],[1,"102","8","Climate Change Adaptation and Disaster Risk Management Knowledge Sharing","Facilitate knowledge sharing: Promote the exchange of information and best practices on climate change adaptation and DRM at the sub-national national, regional, and international levels.",""],[1,"102","11","Capacity Building for Climate and Disaster Risk Management Funding Access","Strengthen institutional and local capacity for accessing funds: Build the capacity of national institutions and local NGOS and community-based associations to develop proposals and concept notes on identified and agreed on CC and DRM at the community, island, and institutional/organizational levels, targeting multiple and flexible community grants and established facilities.",""],[1,"102","12","Climate and Disaster Risk Reduction Partnerships","Foster partnerships: Collaborate with international organizations, development partners, the private sector and local communities to leverage financial and technical resources for climate and disaster risk reduction action.",""],[1,"102","13","Innovative Climate and Disaster Risk Financing Instruments","Explore innovative financing instruments for CC and DRM: Investigate opportunities for innovative financing approaches, such as public-private partnerships, parametric insurance, swap loan, climate bonds to name a few.",""]],"24":[[1,"92","3","Solid Waste Management Project","The Ministry, with the support of MFAT continues to deliver major activities to improve waste management through the Solid waste management project which primarily focused on improving waste management system and ensuring the use of the system by the local people.","The Ministry | MFAT"],[1,"93","3","Hazardous Waste Management Capacity-Building Support","Efforts to enhance the proper management of these wastes require special technical expertise in which the Ministry continues to receive major support from regional partners who provide training to improve the capacity of the local staff on how these wastes are handled to minimize impacts on the environment.","the Ministry"],[1,"93","3","Kaoki-Maange Recycling Scheme","This initiative is known as the Kaoki-Maange recycling scheme, which was established in 2004, and it is currently ongoing involving mainly the collection of aluminum cans, PET bottle and batteries.",""],[1,"94","4","Environmental Compliance Enforcement and Reporting","Enforcement and increasing compliance with proper environment and sustainable development practices.",""],[1,"103","3","Waste Collection, Disposal, and Recycling Improvement","Controlling pollution and environmental degradation through improving waste collection, disposal and recycling for solid and hazardous waste.",""],[1,"103","3","Environmental Awareness and Behavior Change Campaigns","This highlights the importance of delivering massive awareness programs aimed at changing behaviors to allow people to adopt proper environmental practices that include proper disposal of waste using the rubbish collection system currently run by the Councils and other private green bag operators.",""],[1,"103","3","Outer Islands Waste Management Infrastructure Support","The provision of infrastructure to promote proper waste management in the outer islands and leveraging capacities of the authorities who are responsible with waste collection and management are also crucial areas that need ongoing support to address waste management problems in the country.",""],[1,"103","5","Waste Material Export Market Development","There is also a need to explore opportunities on how to address current constraints related to the export of waste materials by finding new buyers to import the PET bottles, used oil and other waste products.",""],[1,"131","1","Waste Oil Processing Plant Installation","installation of a 'Waste Oil Processing Plant' to process and convert the waste oil to clean oil for re-use and re-selling by KOIL",""],[1,"150","35","Waste Collection, Disposal, and Recycling Improvement","Control and reduce environmental pollution through improving waste collection, enhancing proper disposal and recycling services",""],[1,"151","5","Hazardous Waste Management Improvement","Control and reduce environmental pollution through improved management of hazardous wastes",""]],"25":[[1,"8","2","Integrated Domestic Farming Systems Strengthening","Strengthen and integrate domestic farming systems guided by traditional ecological knowledge, to ensure access to a consistent supply of healthy and nutritious food, utilizing sector-specific approaches do not compromise, and where possible build, environmental resilience to climate change impacts.",""],[1,"97","1","Community Engagement in Agricultural Activities Programme","The Agriculture and Livestock Division (ALD) has implemented major programs to promote and strengthen community engagement in agricultural activities nationwide, despite limited budgetary resources.","Agriculture and Livestock Division (ALD)"],[1,"97","1","KOIFAWP Food and Water Security Project","Our major food and water security projects, such as KOIFAWP, LDCF Food Security in the Face of Climate Change, and Kiribati-Chinese Agriculture and Aquaculture Technical Assistance, have significantly contributed to achieving the expected outcomes.",""],[1,"97","1","LDCF Food Security in the Face of Climate Change Project","Our major food and water security projects, such as KOIFAWP, LDCF Food Security in the Face of Climate Change, and Kiribati-Chinese Agriculture and Aquaculture Technical Assistance, have significantly contributed to achieving the expected outcomes.",""],[1,"97","1","Kiribati-Chinese Agriculture and Aquaculture Technical Assistance","Our major food and water security projects, such as KOIFAWP, LDCF Food Security in the Face of Climate Change, and Kiribati-Chinese Agriculture and Aquaculture Technical Assistance, have significantly contributed to achieving the expected outcomes.",""],[1,"97","2","Outer Islands Agricultural Support Programme","Over the past four years, the ALD implemented agricultural programs through Agricultural Assistants and Nurserymen across all the outer islands in Kiribati.",""],[1,"97","2","Free Distribution of Planting Materials","These include the mass production and distribution of planting materials to the communities free of charge,",""],[1,"97","2","Community and School Agricultural Engagement Programme","promoting and enhancing community and school engagements in agricultural activities through training, selling of piglets and chicks for subsistence meat, and egg production, selling of live pigs that do not serve the purpose of breeding and animal health services.",""],[1,"98","5","Technical Assistance and Agricultural Tools for Organic Farmers Associations","They also supported the growth of the Kiribati Organic Farmers Associations by providing ongoing technical assistance and agricultural tools.",""],[1,"98","5","Expanded Food Security Support and Investment","However, to continue this progress, further investments and support are needed to overcome the challenges of expanding these programs and reaching more people who are interested in growing food crops and raising livestock.",""],[1,"104","2","Domestic Farming Systems Strengthening and Integration","Strengthen and integrate domestic farming systems guided by traditional ecological knowledge, to ensure access to a consistent supply of healthy and nutritious food, utilizing sector-specific approaches do not compromise, and where possible build, environmental resilience to climate change impacts.",""],[1,"104","3","Smart Climate Farming and Resilient Crop Production Support","Efforts are required to address the major challenges hindering the expansion of agricultural productions that include the use of smart climate farming approaches to allow farmers to focus on growing more resilient crops",""],[1,"104","3","Farmer Capacity Building in Organic Composting","developing the capacity of farmers in how to make and use organic composing",""],[1,"104","3","Safe Water and Irrigation Access Support for Farmers","Support is also required to allow farmers to access safe water resources to proper irrigation systems to increase and sustain crop productivity",""],[1,"104","4","Agriculture and Livestock Department Capacity Strengthening","strengthening the capacity of the Agriculture and Livestock department (ALD) is also required to allow them to provide agricultural and livestock services needed by farmers in all the Outer Islands.",""],[1,"104","4","Agricultural Equipment and Training Support","This is in the form of providing resources such as equipment, including training in areas that are vital for improving and expanding food crops and livestock production in the country.",""],[1,"104","4","Local Feed Production Development","Investment is also required in exploring opportunities to maximize production of the local feeds appropriate for the pigs and poultry.",""],[1,"104","6","Integrated Domestic Farming Support and Production Expansion","The main targeted areas are agriculture (food crops) and livestock aimed at expanding the current production level through leveraging the support required by farmers and enhancing the capacity of the Agriculture and Livestock Division (ALD) to continue delivering the support needed by farmers.",""],[1,"151","22","Domestic Farming Systems Strengthening and Integration","Strengthen and integrate domestic farming systems to ensure access to a consistent supply of healthy and nutrious food, utilizing sector-specific approaches and fostering resilient ecosystems",""]],"26":[[1,"9","1","Building Infrastructure Safety and Effectiveness Improvement","2. Provide safer and more effective building infrastructure.",""],[1,"9","2","Marine and Coastal Infrastructure Development and Maintenance","Develop, upgrade, and maintain marine and coastal infrastructure.",""],[1,"9","3","Land Transport Infrastructure Development and Upgrading","Develop, upgrade, and sustain land transport infrastructure.",""],[1,"9","4","Air Transport Infrastructure Enhancement","5. Enhance air transport infrastructure.",""],[1,"64","14","Development Partner Collaboration for Infrastructure Improvement","Collaborate with development partners to improve economic and social infrastructure.",""]],"27":[[1,"9","5","Renewable Energy Supply Improvement","Improve renewable energy supply in compliance with the Energy Act and Regulation.",""],[1,"9","6","Grid Power Supply Strengthening","Strengthen the grid power supply in Kiribati in accordance with the Energy Act and Regulation.",""],[1,"9","7","Appliance Energy Compliance Enforcement","8. Enhance appliances' compliance with Energy Act and Regulation.",""],[1,"63","9","Imported Fossil Fuel Reduction and Green Energy PPP Promotion","The government is committed to reducing reliance on imported fossil fuels to create opportunities for public private partnership in green energy projects.",""],[1,"130","5","Renewable Energy and Energy Efficiency Investment Programme","Investing heavily in renewable energy (RE) systems and energy efficiency (EE) programmes would be very beneficial to Kiribati.",""],[1,"131","2","Solar PV Systems Installation for Desalination and Community Electricity","Installation of Solar PV Systems by KGES to provide power to operate the desalination plants and to provide electricity to the communities at the most vulnerable islets,",""],[1,"131","3","South Tarawa Renewable Energy Project Phase I and II","Implementation of the South Tarawa Renewable Energy Project Phase I and II (STREP) with battery energy storage system (BESS) to increase the PUB's current generation capacity to meet the growing demand of the public, strengthening PUB electricity network and initiating product use of electricity by introducing electric vehicle and charging stations and;",""],[1,"131","4","Distribution of China-Funded Solar Home Systems","Distribution of the China-funded solar home systems to the households in the outer islands.",""],[1,"135","8","Renewable Energy Supply Improvement","Improve the renewable energy supply in compliance with the Energy Act & Regulation",""],[1,"140","8","Implementation of the Energy Act 2022 and Renewable Energy Expansion","Kiribati is currently enacting the new Energy Act 2022, along with its associated regulations, to establish a legal framework for the energy sector.",""],[1,"140","8","Solar Power System Expansion and Equitable Distribution","the Government of Kiribati is intensifying efforts to improve the supply and utilization of renewable energy - particularly solar energy.","MISE"],[1,"140","10","South Tarawa Renewable Energy Project","South Tarawa Renewable Energy Project (STREP) 1 and 2 that will significantly enhance energy security in Kiribati, by reducing reliance on imported fossil fuels and increasing the share of renewable energy in electricity generation.",""],[1,"141","1","Solar PV Electrification for Vulnerable Islets and Institutions","Provision of electricity to the vulnerable islets, boarding schools, island councils, ice plants, church communities through solar PV systems.",""],[1,"141","4","National Grid Power Supply Strengthening Initiative","Kiribati is committed to strengthening the national grid power supply to improve electricity access across the nation.",""],[1,"141","5","Grid Electricity Access Expansion in the Gilbert Islands","targets have been set to increase households access to grid electricity from 60% to 70% in the Gilbert islands.",""],[1,"141","6","Grid Power Supply Expansion Initiative","This KDP is now targeting to increase the proportion of household access to grid power supply from 60% to 70% at the Gilbert group and from 34% to 89% at the Line and Phoenix groups.",""],[1,"141","6","Non-Household Grid Access Expansion","Similar efforts to be applied to non- households whereby targeting to increase the number of non-household access to grid power supply at the Gilbert group from 1,295 to 1,495 at the Gilbert Group and to target 1,700 non-households at the Linnix group.",""],[1,"155","26","Renewable Energy Supply Improvement","Improve the renewable energy supply in compliance with the Energy Act & Regulation",""],[1,"155","31","Grid Power Supply Strengthening","Strengthen the grid power supply in Kiribati in accordance with the Energy Act & Regulation",""]],"28":[[1,"9","8","Communication Technology and Connectivity Access Improvement","Improve access to communication technologies and connectivity.",""],[1,"9","9","Quality Information and E-Services Access Enhancement","10. Enhance access to quality information and e-services for all citizens, government agencies, and external stakeholders.",""],[1,"132","1","Digital Connectivity Expansion","The Digital Transformation Office (DTO) and the Communications Commission of Kiribati (CCK) have closely collaborated to enhance communication services, expanding internet and mobile network access.",""],[1,"132","1","Outer Islands Telecommunications Tower Installation","The installation of additional towers to improve internet and Wi-Fi connectivity in the outer islands reached 90% completion in 2023.",""],[1,"132","4","Mobile Coverage Restoration and Service Reliability Maintenance","Vodafone is currently addressing and will report to the Communications Commission of Kiribati (CCK).",""],[1,"132","4","New Core Station Installation in Aranuka","a new core station was recently installed in Aranuka, which also supports Kuria, so both islands will require re-inspection.",""],[1,"132","4","Mobile Coverage Re-inspection Programme","Inspections for Region 3 (Tabuaeran and Teraina) are planned for later this year.",""],[1,"142","3","Connectivity Policy Framework and Partnership Development","A well-designed policy framework and strong partnerships with government, non-government and the private sector are essential to achieving this goal.",""],[1,"142","3","Digital Inclusion and Connectivity Infrastructure Investment","By prioritizing digital inclusion, enhancing connectivity infrastructure, and investing in fit-for- purpose scalable solutions, we can pave the way for transformative and sustainable connectivity initiatives.",""],[1,"143","5","Outer Islands Connectivity Infrastructure Upgrade","it is essential to improve connectivity infrastructure in the outer islands, ensuring it is climate-resilient and capable of extending coverage to underserved communities",""],[1,"143","5","Digital Literacy Promotion Programme","promoting programs aimed at enhancing digital literacy, enabling citizens to actively engage in digital transformation initiatives and fully benefit from the availability of e- services",""],[1,"143","6","Broadband Access and Digital Connectivity Expansion","Expanded access to communication technologies will result in greater internet and mobile network coverage, allowing more people to stay connected.",""],[1,"143","6","Digital Service Resilience Enhancement","Strengthening broadband access and securing backup connections will enhance the resilience and efficiency of digital services.",""]],"29":[[1,"112","21","Digital Government Implementation","Digital Government to be fully implemented; National Portal and Data sharing will be implemented; however, data security and data breach will be strictly monitored.",""],[1,"112","21","National Portal and Data Sharing Implementation","National Portal and Data sharing will be implemented; however, data security and data breach will be strictly monitored.",""],[1,"112","21","Data Security and Breach Monitoring","data security and data breach will be strictly monitored.",""],[1,"118","6","National Standard Database Development and Updating","MFED through the NSO must develop and update the national standard database ensuring effective implementation by all Ministries to support decision makers in providing accurate and reliable data for transparent reports.","MFED | NSO"],[1,"118","7","Integrated Financial Management Information System Rollout","Through the MFED the Integrated Financial Management Information System (IFMIS) has been implemented, the full roll out to the Outer Islands is expected to be completed by the end of 2025.","MFED"],[1,"118","7","IFMIS Module Strengthening and User Capacity Building","New modules in the system need to be strengthened as well as the capacity building for users.",""],[1,"118","8","Integrated One-Stop Digital Services Portal","Digital Services will be fully implemented in all sectors.",""],[1,"118","11","Population Register Strengthening","The Ministry of Justice through the Civil Registry Office needs to have a well-established and reliable system for its base register (population register) to ensure that all citizens are accounted for in the database to assist policy decisions in social benefits, land ownership, elections and many more.","Ministry of Justice | Civil Registry Office"],[1,"135","12","Quality Information and E-Services Access Enhancement","Enhance access to quality information and e-services for all citizens, government agencies and external stakeholders",""],[1,"142","6","ICT Connectivity and Digital Public Service Expansion","This will involve improving ministries' access to broadband connections, securing backup connections to ensure reliability, expanding internet and mobile network coverage, and increasing public access to government services and information online.",""],[1,"143","2","Kiribati Digital Government Project","The Kiribati Digital Government Project (KDGP) is currently being implemented and is making significant progress.",""],[1,"143","3","Digital Transformation Office","This initiative has led to the establishment of the Digital Transformation Office, which operates under a legal mandate provided by the Digital Government Act 2023.",""],[1,"143","4","Digital Government Interoperability Framework and ICT Architecture","Another key component of the project is establishing a digital government interoperability framework and ICT architecture.",""],[1,"143","6","Online Government Services and Information Access","Additionally, improved access to government services and information online will promote digital inclusion, ensuring that citizens and businesses can easily engage with essential services.",""]],"30":[[1,"130","3","Inter-Island Sea Transport Service Provision","The Kiribati National Shipping Line (KNSL) continues to provide regular monthly inter-island sea transport services to 18 islands using its three existing vessels.",""],[1,"135","5","Marine and Coastal Infrastructure Development and Maintenance","Develop, upgrade and maintain marine and coastal infrastructure",""],[1,"138","4","Port and Wharf Upgrading and Construction Programme","Upgrading existing ports and wharfs on South Tarawa and constructing new wharves and ports in the outer islands, are key solutions to addressing poor connectivity in Kiribati.",""],[1,"138","4","Outer Islands Dredging Equipment Acquisition","Additionally, dredging boat channels and passages in the outer islands is another viable solution but it necessitates the purchase of a dredger machine, which adds to the financial burden on the Government.",""],[1,"138","5","Wharf Survey and Preparation for Construction Works","the Kiribati Port Authority, in collaboration with the Marine Division, has conducted a survey of the Butaritari wharf, there are also plans to carry out similar surveys for the wharves in Tabiteuea and Abemama prior to proper construction works begin",""],[1,"138","6","Outer Islands Shipping Infrastructure Investment","Investment in this infrastructure will support the regularity of shipping services and improve cargo delivery to the Outer Islands, as well as facilitate copra uplift, emergency response, and the transportation of goods to both local and international markets.",""],[1,"138","7","New Wharf Construction and Associated Facilities Programme","The government plans to construct four new wharves and associated facilities, one in South Tarawa and three in the outer islands.",""],[1,"142","4","Marine and Coastal Infrastructure Development Programme","building, upgrading, and sustaining marine and coastal infrastructure.",""],[1,"142","5","Inter-Island Transport Infrastructure and Service Upgrade","Implementing these strategies will lead to enhanced transportation infrastructure and services, improving inter- island connectivity through upgraded ports, wharfs, and additional vessels and aircraft.",""],[1,"155","4","Marine and Coastal Infrastructure Development, Upgrading and Maintenance","Develop, upgrade and maintain marine and coastal infrastructure",""],[1,"155","13","Interisland Seatransport Expansion","Increase in number of vessels operated to improve interisland connectivity through seatransport",""]],"31":[[1,"126","6","Climate-Resilient Transport Infrastructure Development","The Government remains fully committed to supporting national infrastructure development and will continue to pursue potential financing opportunities to advance this priority.",""],[1,"126","6","Kiritimati Island Economic Development Program","The continued support from the WB in enhancing climate-resilient transport infrastructure and stimulates economic growth aligns with the Government of Kiribati's Kiritimati Island Economic Development Program.",""],[1,"138","2","Coastal Protection Infrastructure and Hard Adaptation Measures","National Taskforce on costal protection acknowledged priority to focus on infrastructure and hard adaptation measures for coastal protection, to include land reclamation.",""],[1,"138","2","Coastal Adaptation and Land Reclamation Coordination","The coordination on coastal adaptation and land reclamation projects is underway with interested development partners.",""],[1,"138","7","Marine and Coastal Infrastructure Construction Programme","In addition, eight new marine and coastal infrastructure projects (seawalls, bridges, culverts and causeways) throughout Kiribati are planned, complementing ongoing maintenance activities being carried out by the Office of Te Beretitenti for existing ones.",""],[1,"138","7","Seawall, Bridge, and Causeway Maintenance Programme","Furthermore, maintenance work is scheduled for 35 existing seawalls, bridges, and causeways across both rural and urban locations.",""],[1,"138","7","Seawall, Bridge, and Causeway Rehabilitation Programme","The government also intends to implement rehabilitation works on 19 existing seawalls, bridges, and causeways throughout the country.",""]],"32":[[1,"118","4","Kiribati Audit Office Capacity Strengthening","The capacity of the KAO must be strengthened to better fulfill its mandate.",""],[1,"157","1","Kiribati Development Plan Formulation and Indicator Alignment","Facilitate the formation of the new Kiribati Development Plan (KDP), review past progress for all national documents against regional and international agendas and align all indicators (national and international) in a parallel to the new KDP.",""],[1,"157","2","Unified Reporting Table for National Plan and Regional Commitment M&E","Ensure the formation of the unified reporting table for the Monitoring and Evaluation (M&E) of national plans and regional commitments",""],[1,"157","3","Single Reporting Process for Framework Compliance","Ensure the reporting requirements under the following frameworks are met, with a preference for a single reporting process:",""],[1,"157","16","Dataset Collection Coordination Support","Assisting in the coordination of dataset collection",""],[1,"157","19","KDP Mid-Term Review and SDG VNR Review and Commenting Process","Reviewing and providing comments on the KDP Mid-Term Review and SDG VNR",""],[1,"158","3","Six-Monthly Monitoring and Evaluation Meeting Mechanism","It will have a six-monthly meeting for the purposes of M&E and provide regular updates to the Secretary to Cabinet, Secretary of Finance and Office of Te Beretitenti (OB) and any other interested parties.",""],[1,"158","4","Development Coordination Committee Review Mechanism","The Development Coordination Committee (DCC) will review any work of the DIME Taskforce and National Economic Planning Office (NEPO)/National Statistics Office (NSO) before being tables at Cabinet by Honorable Minister for Finance and Economic Development (MFED).",""],[1,"158","5","Development Progress Review and KDP Formulation Taskforce","The taskforce shall convene as needed to review and monitor development progress and to formulate the KDP.",""],[1,"158","10","DIME Taskforce Performance Monitoring Mechanism","The plan is that we will continue the momentum of this technical working group, the DIME Taskforce, to monitor respective Ministries' performances (MSPs & MOPs) over the years through weekly meetings or through special meetings requested updated from Cabinet.",""],[1,"158","11","DIME Taskforce Establishment","The intention behind the establishment of the DIME taskforce is to continue the momentum of this work, so our progress is continuously updated.",""],[1,"158","12","Ministry and Agency Progress Oversight Taskforce","The taskforce will oversee the progress of each Ministry/ Agency against the list of key activities in the national documents to see how the progress over time.",""],[1,"158","13","Weekly Ministry KPI Ranking and Performance Reporting","The taskforce will rank the Ministry by their KPI achievements on a weekly basis to DCC and Cabinet.",""],[1,"159","1","DIME M&E Framework Implementation and Monitoring Process","This KDP is complemented by the Implementation and Monitoring process of the DIME M & E Framework, which serves as the guide for implementation, monitoring, and reporting of this plan.",""],[1,"159","1","Metadata Monitoring Tool","This includes the Metadata Monitoring tool that was established for the previous KDP (2020-2023) to strengthen monitoring, reporting, and evidence-based decision-making, contributing to the successful implementation of the plan.",""],[1,"159","2","Joint Monitoring and Evaluation Process","The monitoring and evaluation process is a joint effort by NEPO and NSO, with the support and technical input of the DIME Taskforce members.",""],[1,"159","2","Bi-annual Progress Reporting","NEPO will compile an analytical Progress Report on the KDP's national performance on a bi-annual basis.",""],[1,"159","2","KPI Assessment and Evaluation System","NSO will assess and evaluate each KPI, which tracks progress against the strategic activities, outputs, and outcomes specified in the Country Results Framework (Annex 2).",""],[1,"159","2","Country Results Framework for Plan Monitoring","The framework will provide the basis for monitoring the plan.",""],[1,"159","3","KDP Progress Reporting and Quality Assurance Mechanism","At the national level, the Development Coordinating Committee (DCC) will provide quality assurance of the KDP through oversight and approval of the bi-annual progress reports.",""],[1,"159","3","KDP Performance Review Taskforce","The Taskforce will meet on a six-monthly basis to measure the progress of each Ministry/Department against the list of KPIs in the Results Framework.",""],[1,"159","3","Annual SDG Performance Summary Reporting","NEPO will also compile an annual summary report on national performance against the SDGs.","NEPO"],[1,"159","4","Mid-Term Review of the KDP","A Mid-Term Review of the KDP will be carried out after two and a half years of the Plan's implementation.",""],[1,"159","5","Final Plan Evaluation","A final evaluation of the KDP will be conducted after four and a half years of the Plan's implementation.",""]],"33":[[1,"36","4","Teacher Upskilling Through Targeted Training and Professional Development","Continued efforts have been undertaken to upskill the remaining unqualified teachers through targeted training and professional development initiatives.",""],[1,"37","2","Kiribati Teachers College Enrollment Expansion","The MoE has also worked to increase enrollment at Kiribati Teachers College (KTC) to strengthen the education system and address the Pupil-Teacher Ratio (PTR).","MoE"],[1,"45","2","Teacher Quality and School Resource Improvement Strategy","the Government is committed to improving the quality of teachers and school resources to support learning and teaching.",""],[1,"45","2","Teaching Workforce Strengthening Initiative","Strengthening the teaching workforce, improving school leadership, and enhancing institutional capacity are central to this goal.",""],[1,"45","2","School Leadership and Institutional Capacity Enhancement","Strengthening the teaching workforce, improving school leadership, and enhancing institutional capacity are central to this goal.",""],[1,"45","4","Teacher CPD Approach Review and Harmonization","Review and harmonize the current approaches of service providers delivering Continuous Professional Development (CPD) for teachers at all levels (ECCE, Primary, JSS, SSS).",""],[1,"45","5","Teacher Welfare and Service Conditions Improvement","Improve teacher welfare and service conditions.",""],[1,"45","6","Targeted Professional Training for Teachers and School Leaders","Provide targeted professional training for teachers and school leaders across all education levels.",""],[1,"45","7","In-Service Teacher Qualification Upgrading and School Leadership Development","Support qualification upgrading for in-service teachers and leadership development for school heads.",""],[1,"45","8","KTC Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the institutional capacity of the KTC.",""],[1,"45","9","Institutional Strengthening of the Ministry of Education","Institutional strengthening of MoE to improve efficient and effective service delivery.","MoE"],[1,"45","10","Teacher Registration Regulations Implementation","Implement the Teacher Registration Regulations to ensure professional standards and accountability.",""],[1,"45","11","Assessment Mechanisms Enhancement and Expansion","Continue to enhance and expand its existing assessment mechanisms such as (STAKI, KCBE, KSCE and KSSC).",""],[1,"45","13","Educator Training in Inclusive Practices and Counselling","Train educators in inclusive practices, conflict resolution, and basic counselling skills",""],[1,"45","15","Safe School Leadership Initiative","Empower students to lead safe school initiatives",""],[1,"45","18","Student Counselling Support","Give counselling to Students in needs.",""],[1,"45","19","Counselling Sector Strengthening and Capacity-Building","Strengthen and capacitate counselling sector",""],[1,"47","1","Interpreter Skills and Teacher Aide Capacity Building","KIT is building interpreter skills, with team members receiving training through the World Association of Sign Language Interpreters Oceania and addressing the nationwide shortage of trained Teacher Aides and Sign Language Interpreters.",""],[1,"107","3","Culture and Heritage Integration in the National Curriculum","This includes improving and integrating culture and heritage into the national curriculum as well as improving library and archives services.",""],[1,"107","3","Library and Archives Services Improvement","This includes improving and integrating culture and heritage into the national curriculum as well as improving library and archives services.",""]],"34":[[1,"40","4","Police Training Program","The Kiribati Police Service (KPS) continues to strengthen law enforcement capacity through its Police Training Program, which covers basic policing, law, and community safety, with increasing regional collaboration.",""],[1,"40","4","Police Recruitment and Training Efforts","Despite infrastructure and staffing limitations, recruitment and training efforts remain critical to meeting growing national and community security needs.",""],[1,"41","4","Police Recruit Training and Probation Programme","All new recruits undergo a six-month training at the Police Training Center, followed by a two-year probation period before confirmation a permanent constable.",""],[1,"47","17","Police Training Capacity Expansion","Support the re-establishment and expansion of the School of Nursing under MHMS, along with increased intake and capacity in police training.",""],[1,"48","13","Police Capacity Strengthening through Donor-Funded Training","Since 2022, KPS has benefited from United Nations-funded training opportunities, notably in police defense and peacekeeping in South Sudan.","Kiribati Police Service (KPS)"],[1,"48","14","Peacekeeping Capacity-Building and Deployment Support","KPS is actively seeking additional donor support to expand capacity-building efforts.",""],[1,"48","14","South Sudan Peacekeeping Deployment Programme","The peacekeeping program in South Sudan involves one-year deployments where officers engage in community outreach and collaborate with local police to promote peace and reduce crime.",""]],"35":[[1,"70","1","Youth Entrepreneurship and Start-up Support Initiative","It seeks to empower young people and promote equity to become successful entrepreneurs, tackle youth unemployment, promote economic development, and support government initiatives that encourage business start-ups for marginalized citizens.",""],[1,"70","2","Youth Entrepreneur Start-up Loan Scheme","The program provides $500 start-up loans to support young entrepreneurs (micro-businesses) with an interest rate of 3%.",""],[1,"70","5","Support Fund for the Unemployed Loan Repayment Support Scheme","One such strategy involves redirecting funds from the Support Fund for the Unemployed (SFU) to ease borrowers' debt burdens.",""],[1,"70","6","Expansion of Program Access to Outer Islands and Priority Groups","Expansion of the program access to other Outer Islands and to include youth women, people with disabilities and disadvantaged families with DBK agencies.",""],[1,"70","7","Financial Inclusion and Institutional Strengthening Support","Enhancing financial inclusion and institutions including prompt and adequate resource support to the KFSA.",""],[1,"70","9","Loan Schemes and Microfinance Access Support","The loan schemes and microfinances remain key instrument in the government's effort to address critical gaps in financial access for residents of the Outer Islands, many of whom remain excluded from formal banking services due to lack of collateral or formal employment.",""]],"36":[[1,"74","3","Death Certification and ICD-10 Coding Improvement","Moving forward, prioritizing accurate death certification and the proper use of internationally recognized International Classification of Diseases (ICD-10 codes will be essential in addressing this information gap.",""],[1,"75","6","Improved Cause-of-Death Coding and Death Certification System","addressing it should be a priority going forward (i.e., use of proper and acceptable International Classification of Diseases (ICD)-10 codes and information for death certification).",""],[1,"78","8","Health Monitoring, Review and Evaluation Framework","MHMS will monitor, review and evaluate through a monitoring and evaluation framework that comprises 94 indicators (19 of which are core indicators).","MHMS"],[1,"79","2","Policy and Planning Unit Establishment","MHMS, with support from development partners, is in the process of establishing a Policy and Planning Unit (PPU) to fulfil key responsibilities related to legislation, governance, policy and project coordination, planning and budgeting, procurement and monitoring, evaluation, research, and learning functions.","MHMS"],[1,"79","2","Health Sector Policy, Planning, and Coordination Support","The PPU will be supporting MHMS to develop, implement and review legislative, governance and policy frameworks, strategic plans, programs, and projects by providing high quality and timely analysis, advice, coordination, and management of activities, functions.","MHMS"],[1,"81","4","Health Data Infrastructure for Decision-Making","The strategic objectives focus on implementing robust health infrastructure for data processes to inform decision-making, improving equitable access to specialized medical services within and outside Kiribati, and reducing the incidence of antimicrobial resistance infections.",""],[1,"81","5","National Health Information Committee","MHMS has proposed the establishment of a National Health Information Committee to lead and oversight the development of the HIS.","MHMS"],[1,"81","5","Integrated National Health Information Database","A comprehensive database that enables collection, storage, analysis and reporting on all aspects of the healthcare system, including program and financial data, is ideally required.",""],[1,"81","5","Health Information System Interoperability and Contingency Planning","Moreover, systems should be capable of interoperating with other GoK systems such as, for example, civil registration and vital statistics.",""]],"37":[[1,"55","9","Community-Based Fishing Support Measures","The Government recognizes the potential contribution of community-based fishing and related market activities to local livelihoods and will continue to implement targeted support measures to enhance participation, competitiveness, and growth within this sector.",""],[1,"58","1","Transshipment Hub Development in Tarawa and Kiritimati","planned developments of transshipment hubs in Tarawa and Kiritimati are expected to promote fisheries activities and further enhance domestic revenue.",""],[1,"58","1","Betio Port Master Plan for Fisheries and Trade","This includes the master plan for the Betio port currently underway to support fishery sector and trade initiatives.",""],[1,"58","4","Fish Processing Infrastructure Development","The Government is fully committed to focus on establishing fish processing infrastructure, developing aquaculture in the outer islands, and building workforce capacity for sustainable practices.",""],[1,"58","4","Outer Islands Aquaculture Development","The Government is fully committed to focus on establishing fish processing infrastructure, developing aquaculture in the outer islands, and building workforce capacity for sustainable practices.",""],[1,"58","4","Sustainable Fisheries Workforce Capacity Building","The Government is fully committed to focus on establishing fish processing infrastructure, developing aquaculture in the outer islands, and building workforce capacity for sustainable practices.",""],[1,"58","5","Partnership Strengthening for Fisheries Development","Success will depend on strengthening partnerships with regional and international organizations, exploring innovative financing through local equity markets, and expanding technical training programs.",""],[1,"58","5","Innovative Fisheries Financing through Local Equity Markets","Success will depend on strengthening partnerships with regional and international organizations, exploring innovative financing through local equity markets, and expanding technical training programs.",""],[1,"58","5","Technical Training Expansion for Fisheries","Success will depend on strengthening partnerships with regional and international organizations, exploring innovative financing through local equity markets, and expanding technical training programs.",""],[1,"58","8","Vessel Day Scheme","Maximizing economic returns from marine resources and sustainable fisheries development in the pursuit of i) Vessel Day Scheme;",""],[1,"58","8","Marine Bonded Warehouse","ii) Marine Bonded Warehouse;",""],[1,"58","8","Purse Seine Net Mending Yard","iii) Purse Seine Net Mending Yard;",""],[1,"58","8","Marine Stewardship Council Certification","iv) Marine Stewardship Council Certification.",""],[1,"58","9","Sustainable Livelihoods Support for Artisanal and Small-Scale Fishers","Providing support to maximize sustainable livelihoods of artisanal and small-scale fishers.",""],[1,"58","10","Aquatic Resources Culture and Fisheries MCS Strengthening","Promoting and strengthening the culture of aquatic resources and the Monitoring, Control and Surveillance (MCS) schemes and promoting diversification of sustainable and adaptive fishing schemes.",""]],"38":[[1,"59","4","Tourism Niche Products Development and Promotion","To develop and promote tourism niche products (cultural values and eco-tourism);",""],[1,"59","7","Tourism Accommodation and Service Standards Upgrade","Upgrade standards of accommodation, restaurants and tour services.",""],[1,"59","8","Local Hospitality Training Programme","To train locals in hospitality programs to enhance services quality and local employment.",""],[1,"59","9","Tourism Marketing and Promotion Campaign","Tourism campaign and awareness through tourism marketing and promotion.",""]],"39":[[1,"111","1","Judiciary Strengthening and Access to Justice Programme","Additionally, enhancing the Judiciary is vital to improving legal interpretation, promoting human rights, and ensuring efficient court services through access to justice programs.",""],[1,"111","1","Legislative Transparency and Public Reporting Measure","The government should ensure that Standing Committee reports, including those from the Public Accounts Committee and the Business Committees-along with Select Committee reports, are tabled at the Maneaba ni Maungatabu and made accessible to the public.",""],[1,"111","6","Business Standing Committee Development","Development of the Business Standing Committee mandated to assess progress on approved motions and questions by the Government in the Maneaba ni Maungatabu",""],[1,"113","4","Alternative Dispute Resolution and Mediation Implementation","Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR) or Mediation to be implemented.",""],[1,"113","12","Case Backlog Mediation Mechanism","Establishing and implementing mediation to assist with backlog of cases",""],[1,"113","15","Legal Framework Update and Legislative Reform","The Maneaba ni Maungatabu is committed to enhancing the legal framework of Kiribati by updating existing laws in working together with the Office of the Attorney General (OAG) ensuring compliance with international standards.","Office of the Attorney General (OAG)"],[1,"118","2","Public Accounts Committee Audit Oversight and Follow-up Mechanism","The Public Accounts Committee (PAC) of Maneaba ni Maungatabu is tasked to monitor Ministries' and SOEs' audit reports at every Parliamentary session.",""],[1,"118","3","Parliamentary Accountability and Transparency Functions","The Maneaba ni Maungatabu continues to play its vital role in accountability and transparency, by allowing Members (MPs) scrutinize the action of the executive through its parliamentary processes such as questions and motions to the Executive and passing of the yearly Appropriation Bill and other Acts.",""]],"40":[[1,"112","23","Public Participation and Citizen Engagement Mechanisms","mechanisms for citizen engagement, such as public consultations and access to information laws.",""],[1,"113","9","Legal and Policy Review and Harmonization for Inclusion","Reviewing and updating laws, ordinances, and policies to be in line with international laws and to mainstream gender and inclusive of persons with disabilities and the vulnerable groups",""],[1,"121","2","Good Governance Awareness and Advocacy Campaigns","Awareness and advocacy campaigns on good governance could also contribute to empowering citizens to hold leaders accountable and fight for equitable and fair opportunities for the common good of all",""],[1,"157","8","Inclusive Stakeholder Engagement in National Planning and Evaluation","Ensure inclusive and comprehensive stakeholder engagement in the national planning and evaluation processes",""]],"41":[[1,"116","10","Police Accountability and Internal Affairs Management","the Kiribati Police Services (KPS) must be able to fulfill the public's expectations and follow professional standards to manage internal affairs to bring justice and peace to the people.",""],[1,"116","13","KPS Equipment and Capacity Strengthening","The increasing number of pending cases also clearly states the need to strengthen the KPS' equipment and capacity to effectively carry out investigations and prosecution of cases.",""],[1,"118","9","Police Complaints Investigation and Prosecution Improvement","It is essential that the Kiribati Police Service enhances its policies and procedures concerning the investigation and prosecution of public complaints.",""],[1,"118","12","Strengthening Border Control Agencies","As such, strengthening existing border control agencies is a must.",""]],"42":[[1,"147","25","Product Development and Diversification through Value-Added Processing","Encourage product development and diversification through value-added process.",""],[1,"147","31","Outer Islands Processing Centre Expansion","Increase the number of processing centres in the outer islands to facilitate the development of value added products and product diversification",""]],"43":[[1,"127","5","School Water and Sanitation Improvement and Monitoring","To support the growing student population, the Ministry of Education is also actively improving and continuously monitoring access to safe drinking water and sanitation facilities across all education levels, including ECCE, primary, JSS, and SSS, to ensure that each school provides a healthy and conducive learning environment.","Ministry of Education"]],"44":[[1,"149","35","Mental Health, Accident, and Suicide Prevention Programs","Implement preventitive programs for Mental health, Accidents and suicide prevention",""]],"45":[[1,"129","3","Annual Road Maintenance Program","Responsibility for maintaining and cleaning roads and drainage lies with MISE and is carried out through the government-funded annual maintenance program.","MISE"],[1,"129","4","Temporary Road Maintenance in the Outer Islands","MISE has provided temporary but adequate road maintenance as needed.","MISE"],[1,"139","2","South Tarawa Transport Network Improvement Project","The Improvement to South Tarawa Transport Network Project (funded by People's Republic of China PRC and to be constructed by China Railway First Group) which aimed to upgrade the road from Temaiku to Bonriki (Te Kawai ae Boou) and Buota into a geocell sealed road is currently progressed with a target to be completed within this 4- year plan.",""],[1,"139","3","Outer Islands Road Improvement Program","The Butaritari Road Improvement project which includes the re-redesign and rehabilitation works on the Butaritari Nan Teiboo Causeway, is funded by the Kiribati Government under the Outer Islands Infrastructure Program (OIIP), commenced in 2024 under a works contract arrangement, will complete in two and half years.",""],[1,"139","3","Abemama Road Improvement Project","The Abemama Road Improvement project will commence in March 2025.",""],[1,"139","3","Tabiteuea North Road Improvement Project","Tabiteuea North Road Improvement in 2026 as part of phase 1 of the OIIP.",""],[1,"139","3","Nikunau Road Improvement Project","Nikunau Road improvement project under Phase 1 will be completed in the next KDP's period.",""],[1,"139","3","Remaining Outer Islands Road Improvement Phases","The road improvements for the remaining outer islands will be undertaken in the next 3 phases of three to four islands in each phase.",""],[1,"139","6","Traffic Light Installation at Betio Intersection","the Government received first of traffic lights in Kiribati, which will be installed at the important intersection in Betio, adjacent to the building of MICT.",""],[1,"155","15","Land Transport Infrastructure Development, Upgrading and Maintenance","Develop, upgrade and sustain land transport infrastructure",""]],"46":[[1,"131","6","KOIL Fuel Storage Capacity Expansion","the Government has approved projects requiring financial support which includes (1) Increasing KOIL's fuel storage capacity",""],[1,"131","6","PUB Generator Procurement for Reliable Power Supply","the Government has approved projects requiring financial support which includes (2) Procuring two 2.5MW generators within the PUB system to ensure delivery of reliable power service across South Tarawa and Betio",""],[1,"131","6","PUB Powerhouse Construction","construction of the PUB powerhouse must proceed in advance to ensure the facility is ready once the generators become available",""],[1,"135","9","Grid Power Supply Strengthening","Strengthen the grid power supply in Kiribati in accordance with the Energy Act & Regulation",""],[1,"141","2","PUB Generator Maintenance and Capacity Expansion","Maintenance of the existing PUB generators as well as the installation of new generators to improve generation capacity to meet the growing demand.",""],[1,"141","3","Fuel Storage Capacity Expansion and Distribution Logistics Improvement","Installation of more fuel tanks to increase the fuel storage capacity, and to improve logistics for distribution of fuel to avoid fuel shortage on the outer islands.",""],[1,"141","5","PUB Generator Procurement Project","The PUB is currently working in collaboration with its mother ministry, MISE, have developed a project document aiming to seek financial support to purchase two 2.5MW Generators to support the operation of PUB in distributing electricity throughout South Tarawa, Betio and some parts of North Tarawa.","MISE"],[1,"141","7","Energy Regulations for Appliance Efficiency Compliance","These regulations will support greater compliance with energy efficiency standards such as those set by Australia for imported appliances, including refrigerators, freezers, air conditioners and lighting.","Energy Planning Department within MISE"],[1,"141","8","Energy Efficiency and Consumer Protection Regulatory Enforcement","By enforcing these regulations, the government strengthens its commitment to promoting energy efficiency, protecting consumers, and supporting the long-term goal of a sustainable and reliable energy supply in Kiribati.",""],[1,"155","36","Appliance Energy Compliance Enhancement","Enhance appliances' compliance with Energy Act and Regulation",""]]}});